{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T00:55:03.646Z","ordinal":68523,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a205e5-07d1-72b3-b0a4-db59d82d43bb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-e63e1d2b-b494-42c5-a8a4-ef9ea39b50df","process_id":"87574","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git status --short --branch; ps -p 3585387,3585403 -o pid=,etime=,stat= || true; for p in cli/src/core/spine_handlers.ts cli/src/index.ts cli/src/knowledge.ts; do c=\"/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_${p//\\//_}\"; echo \"$p\"; cat \"$c/owner.json\" 2>/dev/null || echo released; done; sed -n '1,220p' docs/XERJ_REFERENCE_CODING.md; sed -n '105,180p' cli/src/knowledge.ts; sed -n '750,815p' cli/src/core/spine_handlers.ts; sed -n '1380,1435p' cli/src/index.ts"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git status --short --branch; ps -p 3585387,3585403 -o pid=,etime=,stat= || true; for p in cli/src/core/spine_handlers.ts cli/src/index.ts cli/src/knowledge.ts; do c=\"/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_${p//\\//_}\"; echo \"$p\"; cat \"$c/owner.json\" 2>/dev/null || echo released; done; sed -n '1,220p' docs/XERJ_REFERENCE_CODING.md; sed -n '105,180p' cli/src/knowledge.ts; sed -n '750,815p' cli/src/core/spine_handlers.ts; sed -n '1380,1435p' cli/src/index.ts"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"## codex/context-maturity-v130...origin/release/v1.3.0\nAM cli/src/core/context_inventory.ts\nM  cli/src/core/state.ts\n M cli/src/repl.ts\nMM cli/src/session.ts\n M cli/src/session_export.ts\n M cli/src/sidecar.ts\n M cli/src/slash/catalog.ts\n M cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts\nAM docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md\n?? cli/test/context_inventory.test.ts\ncli/src/core/spine_handlers.ts\nreleased\ncli/src/index.ts\nreleased\ncli/src/knowledge.ts\nreleased\n# Reference coding with XERJ\n\nThe detail behind the \"Reference coding\" rule in `AGENTS.md`: how to reach the local XERJ node, what to query, and what to leave alone.\n\n- Before non-trivial code with a peer-project analogue (feature, protocol, parser, worktree or provider handling, tool, test harness), query the local XERJ node and record what you took, borrowed or rejected in the PR's \"Reference coding\" section. Exempt: trivial edits, doc-only changes, fixes fully specified by a failing test.\n- XERJ is an owner-host tool, not a project dependency (`docs/v1.1.0/DECISIONS.md` §1). Where it is unavailable (contributor machine, CI), write \"XERJ unavailable: <reason>\" in that section and use `git grep` plus the peer's public source.\n- The node is the user service `xerj` on `http://localhost:9200`; confirm with `systemctl --user is-active xerj` and use that node. Stop a hub with `xerj hub stop`.\n- Corpora: `xerj corpus list`. Retrieval is lexical (BM25), so query with identifiers and words from the code: `xerj code <corpus> \"<words>\" -k 4 --full 600`, `xerj search --prefix <index-prefix> \"<words>\" -k 4`, `xerj def --prefix <prefix> \"<symbol>\"`. The first query can take over a minute; set a timeout.\n- `nexus-cli`, `nexus-core`, `nexus-test`, `nexus-docs` index `origin/main` only (hourly), so open PRs are absent: use `git grep` on your branch.\n- Reference code is read-only inspiration. Follow each result's licence tag; copy verbatim only permissively licensed code, with a citation. Keep XERJ and reference corpora away from held-out evaluation tasks (`docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md`). Keep document text local (`rerank` sends it to a third party). Leave indices you did not create alone.\n- After real use: `xerj feedback --dry-run`, then `xerj feedback --submit --agent \"<model>\" --used-for \"<task>\" --verdict \"<what worked and what did not>\"`, with secrets and private data left out.\n      entries: Array.from(this.entries.values()),\n    };\n\n    try {\n      const nexusDir = path.dirname(this.dbPath);\n      ensurePrivateDir(nexusDir);\n      const protectedData = redactForPersistence(data);\n      writeProtectedTextFile(this.dbPath, JSON.stringify(protectedData, null, 2));\n    } catch {\n      throw new Error(\"Failed to protect or save knowledge graph\");\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Adds or updates a knowledge entry.\n   */\n  public set(\n    key: string,\n    value: string,\n    category: KnowledgeCategory = \"rule\",\n    options?: { confidence?: number; tags?: string[] }\n  ): KnowledgeEntry {\n    if (this.readOnly) {\n      throw new Error(\"Read-only mode violation: mutating knowledge graph is blocked\");\n    }\n    const existing = this.entries.get(key);\n    const now = new Date().toISOString();\n    const entry: KnowledgeEntry = {\n      id: existing ? existing.id : randomUUID(),\n      key,\n      value,\n      category,\n      confidence: options?.confidence ?? (existing ? Math.min(existing.confidence + 0.1, 1.0) : 0.8),\n      createdAt: existing ? existing.createdAt : now,\n      updatedAt: now,\n      tags: options?.tags || existing?.tags || [],\n    };\n\n    this.entries.set(key, entry);\n    this.save();\n    return entry;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Retrieves an entry by key.\n   */\n  public get(key: string): KnowledgeEntry | undefined {\n    return this.entries.get(key);\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Deletes an entry by key or ID.\n   */\n  public delete(keyOrId: string): boolean {\n    if (this.readOnly) {\n      throw new Error(\"Read-only mode violation: mutating knowledge graph is blocked\");\n    }\n    if (this.entries.has(keyOrId)) {\n      this.entries.delete(keyOrId);\n      this.save();\n      return true;\n    }\n\n    for (const [key, entry] of this.entries.entries()) {\n      if (entry.id === keyOrId) {\n        this.entries.delete(key);\n        this.save();\n        return true;\n      }\n    }\n\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Returns all stored entries.\n      const typeRes = await this.browser.type(args.selector || \"\", args.text || \"\");\n      return {\n        success: typeRes.success,\n        output: JSON.stringify(typeRes, null, 2),\n        error: typeRes.success ? undefined : typeRes.message,\n      };\n    } catch (err: any) {\n      return {\n        success: false,\n        output: \"\",\n        error: `Error executing browser_type: ${err.message}`,\n      };\n    }\n  });\n\n  this.spine.registerHandler(\"browser_console_logs\", async (args: any) => {\n    try {\n      const logs = this.browser.getConsoleLogs(args.limit ? parseInt(args.limit, 10) : 50);\n      return {\n        success: true,\n        output: JSON.stringify({ totalLogs: logs.length, logs }, null, 2),\n      };\n    } catch (err: any) {\n      return {\n        success: false,\n        output: \"\",\n        error: `Error executing browser_console_logs: ${err.message}`,\n      };\n    }\n  });\n\n  this.spine.registerHandler(\"manage_knowledge\", async (args: any) => {\n    try {\n      let output = \"\";\n      const action = args.action || \"list\";\n      if (action === \"set\") {\n        const entry = this.knowledge.set(\n          args.key || \"custom-rule\",\n          args.value || \"\",\n          args.category || \"rule\"\n        );\n        output = JSON.stringify({ status: \"saved\", entry }, null, 2);\n      } else if (action === \"get\") {\n        const entry = this.knowledge.get(args.key || \"\");\n        output = JSON.stringify({ found: Boolean(entry), entry }, null, 2);\n      } else if (action === \"delete\") {\n        const deleted = this.knowledge.delete(args.key || \"\");\n        output = JSON.stringify(\n          { status: deleted ? \"deleted\" : \"not_found\", key: args.key },\n          null,\n          2\n        );\n      } else if (action === \"query\") {\n        const entries = this.knowledge.query(args.key || args.value, args.category);\n        output = JSON.stringify({ total: entries.length, entries }, null, 2);\n      } else {\n        const entries = this.knowledge.list();\n        output = JSON.stringify({ total: entries.length, entries }, null, 2);\n      }\n      return { success: true, output };\n    } catch (err: any) {\n      return {\n        success: false,\n        output: \"\",\n        error: `Error executing manage_knowledge: ${err.message}`,\n      };\n        maxMinutes: options.maxMinutes,\n        temperature: options.temperature,\n      }, buildConfig(options));\n      console.log(report.output);\n      console.error(pc.dim(`Structured score saved to ${path.resolve(options.output || \"eval-score.json\")}; run artifacts: ${report.runner.outputDir}`));\n      return;\n    }\n    const config = buildConfig(options);\n    console.log(pc.bold(pc.cyan(`\\n📊 Loading evaluation dataset: ${datasetPath}`)));\n    let instances = BenchmarkEvaluator.loadDataset(datasetPath);\n    if (options.limit) {\n      const limit = parseInt(options.limit, 10);\n      instances = instances.slice(0, limit);\n    }\n    console.log(pc.dim(`Loaded ${instances.length} benchmark task instance(s).`));\n    const evaluator = new BenchmarkEvaluator(config.workspace);\n    const summary = await evaluator.runBenchmark(instances, config);\n    const scorecard = BenchmarkEvaluator.renderScorecard(summary);\n    console.log(\"\\n\" + scorecard);\n    const outputPath = path.resolve(options.output || \"eval-scorecard.md\");\n    fs.writeFileSync(outputPath, scorecard, \"utf-8\");\n    console.log(pc.green(`✔ Scorecard saved to: ${outputPath}\\n`));\n  });\n\nprogram\n  .command(\"knowledge [action] [key] [val...]\")\n  .description(\"Inspect or manage persistent project knowledge graph\")\n  .option(\"-w, --workspace <path>\", \"Workspace directory\", process.cwd())\n  .option(\"-c, --category <type>\", \"Category: idiom, architecture, dependency, troubleshooting, rule\", \"rule\")\n  .action((action: string | undefined, key: string | undefined, valParts: string[] | undefined, options: any) => {\n    const ws = options.workspace ? path.resolve(options.workspace) : process.cwd();\n    const kg = new KnowledgeGraph(ws);\n    const act = (action || \"list\").toLowerCase();\n    if (act === \"set\" && key) {\n      const val = (valParts || []).join(\" \");\n      const entry = kg.set(key, val, options.category);\n      console.log(pc.green(`✔ Saved knowledge entry: [${entry.category}] ${entry.key}`));\n    } else if (act === \"get\" && key) {\n      const entry = kg.get(key);\n      if (entry) {\n        console.log(`\\n• [${pc.cyan(entry.category)}] ${pc.bold(entry.key)}: ${pc.white(entry.value)} (confidence: ${entry.confidence})\\n`);\n      } else {\n        console.log(pc.yellow(`Key '${key}' not found in knowledge graph.\\n`));\n      }\n    } else if (act === \"delete\" && key) {\n      const deleted = kg.delete(key);\n      console.log(deleted ? pc.green(`✔ Deleted entry: ${key}\\n`) : pc.yellow(`Entry not found: ${key}\\n`));\n    } else {\n      const list = kg.list();\n      if (list.length === 0) {\n        console.log(pc.yellow(\"\\nNo persistent knowledge entries found in .nexus/knowledge.json\\n\"));\n        return;\n      }\n      console.log(pc.bold(pc.cyan(`\\n=== Persistent Project Knowledge Graph (${list.length} entries) ===\\n`)));\n      for (const e of list) {\n        console.log(`• [${pc.cyan(e.category)}] ${pc.bold(e.key)}: ${pc.white(e.value)}`);\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":875461555}},"started_at_ms":1795395302770,"completed_at_ms":1795395303646}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T00:55:03.824Z","ordinal":68524,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a205e6-3990-72b3-9b27-95efb3bca4dc","call_id":"call_8aae3e33c47242b8863fa28b8ec2617a","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"## codex/context-maturity-v130...origin/release/v1.3.0\nAM cli/src/core/context_inventory.ts\nM  cli/src/core/state.ts\n M cli/src/repl.ts\nMM cli/src/session.ts\n M cli/src/session_export.ts\n M cli/src/sidecar.ts\n M cli/src/slash/catalog.ts\n M cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts\nAM docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md\n?? cli/test/context_inventory.test.ts\ncli/src/core/spine_handlers.ts\nreleased\ncli/src/index.ts\nreleased\ncli/src/knowledge.ts\nreleased\n# Reference coding with XERJ\n\nThe detail behind the \"Reference coding\" rule in `AGENTS.md`: how to reach the local XERJ node, what to query, and what to leave alone.\n\n- Before non-trivial code with a peer-project analogue (feature, protocol, parser, worktree or provider handling, tool, test harness), query the local XERJ node and record what you took, borrowed or rejected in the PR's \"Reference coding\" section. Exempt: trivial edits, doc-only changes, fixes fully specified by a failing test.\n- XERJ is an owner-host tool, not a project dependency (`docs/v1.1.0/DECISIONS.md` §1). Where it is unavailable (contributor machine, CI), write \"XERJ unavailable: <reason>\" in that section and use `git grep` plus the peer's public source.\n- The node is the user service `xerj` on `http://localhost:9200`; confirm with `systemctl --user is-active xerj` and use that node. Stop a hub with `xerj hub stop`.\n- Corpora: `xerj corpus list`. Retrieval is lexical (BM25), so query with identifiers and words from the code: `xerj code <corpus> \"<words>\" -k 4 --full 600`, `xerj search --prefix <index-prefix> \"<words>\" -k 4`, `xerj def --prefix <prefix> \"<symbol>\"`. The first query can take over a minute; set a timeout.\n- `nexus-cli`, `nexus-core`, `nexus-test`, `nexus-docs` index `origin/main` only (hourly), so open PRs are absent: use `git grep` on your branch.\n- Reference code is read-only inspiration. Follow each result's licence tag; copy verbatim only permissively licensed code, with a citation. Keep XERJ and reference corpora away from held-out evaluation tasks (`docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md`). Keep document text local (`rerank` sends it to a third party). Leave indices you did not create alone.\n- After real use: `xerj feedback --dry-run`, then `xerj feedback --submit --agent \"<model>\" --used-for \"<task>\" --verdict \"<what worked and what did not>\"`, with secrets and private data left out.\n      entries: Array.from(this.entries.values()),\n    };\n\n    try {\n      const nexusDir = path.dirname(this.dbPath);\n      ensurePrivateDir(nexusDir);\n      const protectedData = redactForPersistence(data);\n      writeProtectedTextFile(this.dbPath, JSON.stringify(protectedData, null, 2));\n    } catch {\n      throw new Error(\"Failed to protect or save knowledge graph\");\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Adds or updates a knowledge entry.\n   */\n  public set(\n    key: string,\n    value: string,\n    category: KnowledgeCategory = \"rule\",\n    options?: { confidence?: number; tags?: string[] }\n  ): KnowledgeEntry {\n    if (this.readOnly) {\n      throw new Error(\"Read-only mode violation: mutating knowledge graph is blocked\");\n    }\n    const existing = this.entries.get(key);\n    const now = new Date().toISOString();\n    const entry: KnowledgeEntry = {\n      id: existing ? existing.id : randomUUID(),\n      key,\n      value,\n      category,\n      confidence: options?.confidence ?? (existing ? Math.min(existing.confidence + 0.1, 1.0) : 0.8),\n      createdAt: existing ? existing.createdAt : now,\n      updatedAt: now,\n      tags: options?.tags || existing?.tags || [],\n    };\n\n    this.entries.set(key, entry);\n    this.save();\n    return entry;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Retrieves an entry by key.\n   */\n  public get(key: string): KnowledgeEntry | undefined {\n    return this.entries.get(key);\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Deletes an entry by key or ID.\n   */\n  public delete(keyOrId: string): boolean {\n    if (this.readOnly) {\n      throw new Error(\"Read-only mode violation: mutating knowledge graph is blocked\");\n    }\n    if (this.entries.has(keyOrId)) {\n      this.entries.delete(keyOrId);\n      this.save();\n      return true;\n    }\n\n    for (const [key, entry] of this.entries.entries()) {\n      if (entry.id === keyOrId) {\n        this.entries.delete(key);\n        this.save();\n        return true;\n      }\n    }\n\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Returns all stored entries.\n      const typeRes = await this.browser.type(args.selector || \"\", args.text || \"\");\n      return {\n        success: typeRes.success,\n        output: JSON.stringify(typeRes, null, 2),\n        error: typeRes.success ? undefined : typeRes.message,\n      };\n    } catch (err: any) {\n      return {\n        success: false,\n        output: \"\",\n        error: `Error executing browser_type: ${err.message}`,\n      };\n    }\n  });\n\n  this.spine.registerHandler(\"browser_console_logs\", async (args: any) => {\n    try {\n      const logs = this.browser.getConsoleLogs(args.limit ? parseInt(args.limit, 10) : 50);\n      return {\n        success: true,\n        output: JSON.stringify({ totalLogs: logs.length, logs }, null, 2),\n      };\n    } catch (err: any) {\n      return {\n        success: false,\n        output: \"\",\n        error: `Error executing browser_console_logs: ${err.message}`,\n      };\n    }\n  });\n\n  this.spine.registerHandler(\"manage_knowledge\", async (args: any) => {\n    try {\n      let output = \"\";\n      const action = args.action || \"list\";\n      if (action === \"set\") {\n        const entry = this.knowledge.set(\n          args.key || \"custom-rule\",\n          args.value || \"\",\n          args.category || \"rule\"\n        );\n        output = JSON.stringify({ status: \"saved\", entry }, null, 2);\n      } else if (action === \"get\") {\n        const entry = this.knowledge.get(args.key || \"\");\n        output = JSON.stringify({ found: Boolean(entry), entry }, null, 2);\n      } else if (action === \"delete\") {\n        const deleted = this.knowledge.delete(args.key || \"\");\n        output = JSON.stringify(\n          { status: deleted ? \"deleted\" : \"not_found\", key: args.key },\n          null,\n          2\n        );\n      } else if (action === \"query\") {\n        const entries = this.knowledge.query(args.key || args.value, args.category);\n        output = JSON.stringify({ total: entries.length, entries }, null, 2);\n      } else {\n        const entries = this.knowledge.list();\n        output = JSON.stringify({ total: entries.length, entries }, null, 2);\n      }\n      return { success: true, output };\n    } catch (err: any) {\n      return {\n        success: false,\n        output: \"\",\n        error: `Error executing manage_knowledge: ${err.message}`,\n      };\n        maxMinutes: options.maxMinutes,\n        temperature: options.temperature,\n      }, buildConfig(options));\n      console.log(report.output);\n      console.error(pc.dim(`Structured score saved to ${path.resolve(options.output || \"eval-score.json\")}; run artifacts: ${report.runner.outputDir}`));\n      return;\n    }\n    const config = buildConfig(options);\n    console.log(pc.bold(pc.cyan(`\\n📊 Loading evaluation dataset: ${datasetPath}`)));\n    let instances = BenchmarkEvaluator.loadDataset(datasetPath);\n    if (options.limit) {\n      const limit = parseInt(options.limit, 10);\n      instances = instances.slice(0, limit);\n    }\n    console.log(pc.dim(`Loaded ${instances.length} benchmark task instance(s).`));\n    const evaluator = new BenchmarkEvaluator(config.workspace);\n    const summary = await evaluator.runBenchmark(instances, config);\n    const scorecard = BenchmarkEvaluator.renderScorecard(summary);\n    console.log(\"\\n\" + scorecard);\n    const outputPath = path.resolve(options.output || \"eval-scorecard.md\");\n    fs.writeFileSync(outputPath, scorecard, \"utf-8\");\n    console.log(pc.green(`✔ Scorecard saved to: ${outputPath}\\n`));\n  });\n\nprogram\n  .command(\"knowledge [action] [key] [val...]\")\n  .description(\"Inspect or manage persistent project knowledge graph\")\n  .option(\"-w, --workspace <path>\", \"Workspace directory\", process.cwd())\n  .option(\"-c, --category <type>\", \"Category: idiom, architecture, dependency, troubleshooting, rule\", \"rule\")\n  .action((action: string | undefined, key: string | undefined, valParts: string[] | undefined, options: any) => {\n    const ws = options.workspace ? path.resolve(options.workspace) : process.cwd();\n    const kg = new KnowledgeGraph(ws);\n    const act = (action || \"list\").toLowerCase();\n    if (act === \"set\" && key) {\n      const val = (valParts || []).join(\" \");\n      const entry = kg.set(key, val, options.category);\n      console.log(pc.green(`✔ Saved knowledge entry: [${entry.category}] ${entry.key}`));\n    } else if (act === \"get\" && key) {\n      const entry = kg.get(key);\n      if (entry) {\n        console.log(`\\n• [${pc.cyan(entry.category)}] ${pc.bold(entry.key)}: ${pc.white(entry.value)} (confidence: ${entry.confidence})\\n`);\n      } else {\n        console.log(pc.yellow(`Key '${key}' not found in knowledge graph.\\n`));\n      }\n    } else if (act === \"delete\" && key) {\n      const deleted = kg.delete(key);\n      console.log(deleted ? pc.green(`✔ Deleted entry: ${key}\\n`) : pc.yellow(`Entry not found: ${key}\\n`));\n    } else {\n      const list = kg.list();\n      if (list.length === 0) {\n        console.log(pc.yellow(\"\\nNo persistent knowledge entries found in .nexus/knowledge.json\\n\"));\n        return;\n      }\n      console.log(pc.bold(pc.cyan(`\\n=== Persistent Project Knowledge Graph (${list.length} entries) ===\\n`)));\n      for (const e of list) {\n        console.log(`• [${pc.cyan(e.category)}] ${pc.bold(e.key)}: ${pc.white(e.value)}`);\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a205e5-07d1-72b3-b0a4-db59d82d43bb","create_time":1795395303.82411}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":30316,"sampled_through_sequence":30308,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
