{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T00:57:33.722Z","ordinal":68588,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a205e5-07d1-72b3-b0a4-db59d82d43bb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-177bbb4d-2864-457f-8a27-330e99d2da3e","process_id":"9175","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n \"manage_knowledge|registerHandler\\(.*knowledge|spine.*handler|dispatchToolCall\\(.*manage_knowledge\" cli/test --glob '*.test.ts' | head -100; sed -n '1,180p' cli/src/core/capability_definitions/knowledge.ts; rg -n 'AUTOEXTRACT' cli docs"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n \"manage_knowledge|registerHandler\\\\(.*knowledge|spine.*handler|dispatchToolCall\\\\(.*manage_knowledge\" cli/test --glob '*.test.ts'","query":"manage_knowledge|registerHandler\\(.*knowledge|spine.*handler|dispatchToolCall\\(.*manage_knowledge","path":"test"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,180p' cli/src/core/capability_definitions/knowledge.ts","name":"knowledge.ts","path":"cli/src/core/capability_definitions/knowledge.ts"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n AUTOEXTRACT cli docs","query":"AUTOEXTRACT","path":"cli"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"cli/test/tool_groups.test.ts:22:    for (const hidden of [\"browser_navigate\", \"lsp_hover\", \"search_web\", \"fetch_web\", \"hybrid_search\", \"manage_knowledge\"]) assert.ok(!offered.includes(hidden), hidden);\ncli/test/role_deny_lists.test.ts:32:  assert.deepEqual([...roleToolDenyList(\"implementer\")!].sort(), [...BROWSER, \"manage_knowledge\"].sort());\ncli/test/role_deny_lists.test.ts:33:  assert.deepEqual([...roleToolDenyList(\"tester\")!].sort(), [...BROWSER, \"manage_knowledge\", \"fetch_web\", \"search_web\", \"spawn_subagent\"].sort());\ncli/test/role_deny_lists.test.ts:40:  [\"implementer\", [...BROWSER, \"manage_knowledge\"]],\ncli/test/role_deny_lists.test.ts:41:  [\"tester\", [...BROWSER, \"manage_knowledge\", \"fetch_web\", \"search_web\", \"spawn_subagent\"]],\ncli/test/role_deny_lists.test.ts:65:  for (const name of [\"fetch_web\", \"search_web\", \"manage_knowledge\", \"browser_navigate\"]) assert.equal(offered.has(name), true, `${name} for no role`);\ncli/test/verification_outcome.test.ts:109:      // spine_handlers.ts (the completion oracle): the change stops being pending only after a passing run that\ncli/test/verify_typecheck_guard.test.ts:80:    // spine_handlers.ts: the verifier's pass does not count, and independence is not judged.\ncli/test/spine.test.ts:137:    spine.registerHandler(\"manage_knowledge\", async () => {\ncli/test/spine.test.ts:143:      { toolName: \"manage_knowledge\", args: { action: \"set\", key: \"k\", value: \"v\" } },\ncli/test/turn_verdict_evidence.test.ts:79:const knowledge = { kind: \"tools\" as const, calls: [{ name: \"manage_knowledge\", args: { action: \"set\", key: \"k\", value: \"v\" } }] };\ncli/test/capabilities.test.ts:62:      \"manage_knowledge\",\ncli/test/ceri_semantic_integrity.test.ts:458:    spine.registerHandler(\"mcp__s__push\", async () => { handlerCalls++; return { success: true, output: \"real\" }; });\ncli/test/capability_workspace_effects.test.ts:26:  const knowledge = registry.getByToolName(\"manage_knowledge\");\ncli/test/capability_workspace_effects.test.ts:28:  assert.equal(changesWorkspace(knowledge), true, \"manage_knowledge writes .nexus/knowledge.json in the workspace\");\ncli/test/approval_policy.test.ts:27:  manage_knowledge: \"write_workspace\",\nimport type { CanonicalCapability } from \"../capabilities.js\";\n\nexport const manageKnowledgeCapability: CanonicalCapability = {\n  \"id\": \"knowledge_store\",\n  \"modelToolName\": \"manage_knowledge\",\n  \"category\": \"knowledge\",\n  \"mutating\": true,\n  \"effect\": \"write_workspace\",\n  \"sideEffectContract\": \"Store, retrieve, query or delete persistent knowledge entries\",\n  \"backend\": \"ts_native\",\n  \"toolDefinition\": {\n    \"type\": \"function\",\n    \"function\": {\n      \"name\": \"manage_knowledge\",\n      \"description\": \"Query or record persistent project idioms, rules, dependencies, and architectural decisions.\",\n      \"parameters\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"action\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"enum\": [\n              \"get\",\n              \"set\",\n              \"list\",\n              \"delete\",\n              \"query\"\n            ],\n            \"description\": \"The knowledge operation to execute.\"\n          },\n          \"key\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Knowledge entry key identifier (e.g. 'preferred-package-manager').\"\n          },\n          \"value\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Value or rule description to persist.\"\n          },\n          \"category\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"enum\": [\n              \"idiom\",\n              \"architecture\",\n              \"dependency\",\n              \"troubleshooting\",\n              \"rule\"\n            ],\n            \"description\": \"Classification category for the knowledge entry.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"action\"\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  }\n};\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:184:**Chosen:** off by default; opt-in with `NEXUS_KNOWLEDGE_AUTOEXTRACT=1`, with a visible notice each time a rule is saved. Workspace knowledge is loaded only when the workspace is trusted.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:61:- Automatic knowledge extraction (`autoExtract`) is disabled by default (DEC-15). It can be enabled with `NEXUS_KNOWLEDGE_AUTOEXTRACT=1`, which issues a notification when new rules are persisted.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md:44:   - `autoExtract` is removed, or opt-in through `NEXUS_KNOWLEDGE_AUTOEXTRACT=1` with a visible notice each time a rule is saved;\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:769:- **Knowledge Graph Hygiene & Auto-Extraction Gating (REQ-SEC-114)**: The `KnowledgeGraph` has a lazy constructor that performs no filesystem creation until a write is explicitly requested. In `--read-only` mode, all mutations are blocked. Implicit standing instruction creation via automatic prompt mining (`autoExtract`) is disabled by default per DEC-15. It can only be enabled explicitly via `NEXUS_KNOWLEDGE_AUTOEXTRACT=1`, which prints a notification whenever a new rule is recorded into `<workspace>/.nexus/knowledge.json`.\ncli/test/workspace_trust.test.ts:23:  const saved = { HOME: process.env.HOME, TRUST: process.env.NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE, AUTO: process.env.NEXUS_KNOWLEDGE_AUTOEXTRACT };\ncli/test/workspace_trust.test.ts:26:  delete process.env.NEXUS_KNOWLEDGE_AUTOEXTRACT;\ncli/test/workspace_trust.test.ts:33:    if (saved.AUTO === undefined) delete process.env.NEXUS_KNOWLEDGE_AUTOEXTRACT;\ncli/test/workspace_trust.test.ts:34:    else process.env.NEXUS_KNOWLEDGE_AUTOEXTRACT = saved.AUTO;\ncli/test/workspace_trust.test.ts:242:      // 1. Default config: NEXUS_KNOWLEDGE_AUTOEXTRACT is unset\ncli/test/workspace_trust.test.ts:243:      delete process.env.NEXUS_KNOWLEDGE_AUTOEXTRACT;\ncli/test/workspace_trust.test.ts:266:      // 2. Opt-in via NEXUS_KNOWLEDGE_AUTOEXTRACT=1\ncli/test/workspace_trust.test.ts:267:      process.env.NEXUS_KNOWLEDGE_AUTOEXTRACT = \"1\";\ncli/test/workspace_trust.test.ts:271:      delete process.env.NEXUS_KNOWLEDGE_AUTOEXTRACT;\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:92:- The existing operator `/knowledge set` is an explicit write path, but `manage_knowledge` also lets model-generated tool arguments call `KnowledgeGraph.set`; legacy `autoExtract` can write prompt-derived entries when `NEXUS_KNOWLEDGE_AUTOEXTRACT=1`. This context slice did not change those paths because `core/spine_handlers.ts`, `index.ts`, and `agent.ts` are owned by the active GV-1 slice. A boundary request asks that owner to require operator confirmation and preserve provenance/validation metadata. Until that is done, do not enable automatic extraction, and treat every persisted entry as unverified memory rather than evidence. Deletion/expiry enforcement, live provider calls, and held-out task-quality evaluation were not added.\ncli/src/knowledge.ts:237:   * Opt-in only via NEXUS_KNOWLEDGE_AUTOEXTRACT=1 (REQ-SEC-114).\ncli/src/knowledge.ts:241:    if (this.readOnly || process.env.NEXUS_KNOWLEDGE_AUTOEXTRACT !== \"1\") {\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md:34:| 7 | Knowledge: lazy constructor (no `mkdir`), no writes in read-only mode, `autoExtract` behind `NEXUS_KNOWLEDGE_AUTOEXTRACT=1` with a notice. | `knowledge.ts:34-43,206-231`; `agent.ts:4934-4936` | — |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":129615177}},"started_at_ms":1795395452592,"completed_at_ms":1795395453722}}
