{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T01:03:12.780Z","ordinal":68752,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0f4fd85789ec756b016b0390bbe2ec87d2aa8f040d1735c3bd","status":"completed","call_id":"call_ce8c7163a093479c988f3e47112c63af","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130/docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md\\n@@\\n-- `ContextInventoryItem`: stable source-identity id (source type + location + scope; no content hash is persisted), source kind/location, estimated tokens, observed time, freshness (`current`, `stale`, `unknown`), trust state, retention, inclusion reason, retrieval method, and optional source references.\\n+- `ContextInventoryItem`: stable source-identity id (source type + location + scope; no content hash is persisted), source kind/location, estimated tokens, observed time, freshness (`current`, `stale`, `unknown`), trust state, retention, inclusion reason, retrieval method, and optional source references. Message and tool-call identifiers are retained only as opaque hashes.\\n@@\\n - Inventory collection is local and read-only. Failed or unsupported sources are reported with explicit partial status.\\n+- Durable project knowledge is promoted only through explicit operator commands. Model-invoked `manage_knowledge` rejects `set` even through the internal handler, and the model-visible schema omits that action. Legacy conversation auto-extraction is a no-op, including when its old environment flag is present.\\n+- Knowledge entries retain repository scope, provenance, validation status, timestamps, and retention policy. Legacy entries migrate additively as `legacy_unverified`; expiring entries are removed from retrieval and pruned on load. Prompt injection labels all knowledge as unverified memory, never evidence. Secret-bearing values are rejected before entering the prompt-visible map.\\n@@\\n 7. No provider changes, provider-specific headers, or new service dependencies are added.\\n+8. Model tool calls and legacy automatic extraction cannot promote durable memory; operator-created knowledge carries provenance and explicit unverified validation status, and expired entries are not retrieved.\\n@@\\n-- Automatic durable-memory promotion, retrieval ranking changes, and context eviction remain deferred. Existing validation research (`CONTEXT-ENGINEERING-VALIDATION-PLAN.md`) says to validate bounded ingestion and evidence reuse before adopting more complex retrieval policies.\\n+- Automatic memory learning, retrieval ranking changes, and context eviction remain deferred. Durable promotion is operator-only; accumulated memory has not yet been shown to improve task quality on held-out work.\\n@@\\n-XERJ retrieval on `nexus-cli` located the existing context admission/token-accounting path in `cli/src/agent.ts` (`requestMessages`, `admitContext`) and the durable note provenance logic in the same file, plus the project knowledge graph in `cli/src/knowledge.ts`. The implementation reuses those boundaries and adds a local diagnostic; it rejects adding a second planner, a provider-specific context protocol, or an external retrieval service. XERJ's index reflects committed `origin/main`, so current worktree details were checked directly in source. No reference-project code was copied.\\n+XERJ retrieval on `nexus-cli` located the existing context admission/token-accounting path in `cli/src/agent.ts` (`requestMessages`, `admitContext`), the `manage_knowledge` capability (`cli/src/core/capability_definitions/knowledge.ts:23`), and the local project knowledge graph (`cli/src/knowledge.ts:37-45`). OpenCode results showed permission checks belong at the application boundary; Goose results offered no relevant durable-memory analogue. Nexus therefore keeps the existing `KnowledgeGraph`, removes model-write affordances at both schema and handler, and uses the existing operator CLI as the promotion boundary. It rejects a second planner, provider-specific context protocol, external retrieval service, or copied peer implementation. XERJ indexes committed `origin/main`; the active worktree was checked directly.\\n@@\\n-- Exact request-time context capture is blocked by the active `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts` ownership claim. A bounded handoff request was recorded in the shared claims log; the current owner is not registered in Agent Mail, so delivery through that channel was unavailable. The diagnostic and persisted snapshots explicitly remain partial until the owner releases the file or applies the small integration.\\n+- Exact request-time context capture remains pending under an active `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts` claim. A handoff was recorded and the prior GV-1 owner released the memory handler paths; request construction remains explicitly partial until the current agent owner releases or applies that integration.\\n@@\\n-- The existing operator `/knowledge set` is an explicit write path, but `manage_knowledge` also lets model-generated tool arguments call `KnowledgeGraph.set`; legacy `autoExtract` can write prompt-derived entries when `NEXUS_KNOWLEDGE_AUTOEXTRACT=1`. This context slice did not change those paths because `core/spine_handlers.ts`, `index.ts`, and `agent.ts` are owned by the active GV-1 slice. A boundary request asks that owner to require operator confirmation and preserve provenance/validation metadata. Until that is done, do not enable automatic extraction, and treat every persisted entry as unverified memory rather than evidence. Deletion/expiry enforcement, live provider calls, and held-out task-quality evaluation were not added.\\n+- Operator-only memory promotion now carries metadata and expiry enforcement, but no held-out task-quality evaluation establishes that durable memories improve results. Existing schema-1 records are migrated additively when a writable load occurs; read-only loads label them in memory without rewriting their files.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a205e5-07d1-72b3-b0a4-db59d82d43bb","create_time":1795395771.9416966}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":30417,"sampled_through_sequence":30415,"client_authored":false}}
