{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T01:03:20.198Z","ordinal":68759,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0f4fd85789ec756b016b0390d25fb087d28bdb81ddfad51212","status":"completed","call_id":"call_826b5ee6cae34f07af2fa8a29ccf8bee","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130/docs/USER_MANUAL.md\\n@@\\n-- **Knowledge Graph Hygiene & Auto-Extraction Gating (REQ-SEC-114)**: The `KnowledgeGraph` has a lazy constructor that performs no filesystem creation until a write is explicitly requested. In `--read-only` mode, all mutations are blocked. Implicit standing instruction creation via automatic prompt mining (`autoExtract`) is disabled by default per DEC-15. It can only be enabled explicitly via `NEXUS_KNOWLEDGE_AUTOEXTRACT=1`, which prints a notification whenever a new rule is recorded into `<workspace>/.nexus/knowledge.json`.\\n+- **Knowledge Graph Hygiene & Controlled Promotion (REQ-SEC-114)**: The `KnowledgeGraph` has a lazy constructor that performs no filesystem creation until a write is explicitly requested. In `--read-only` mode, all mutations are blocked. Promote durable project knowledge only through an explicit operator command: `/knowledge set <key> <rule>` or `nexus knowledge set <key> <value>`. Model calls to `manage_knowledge` cannot set entries, and the legacy `NEXUS_KNOWLEDGE_AUTOEXTRACT` flag no longer enables conversation-derived writes. Entries are scoped to the workspace, retain provenance and validation status, expire according to their retention policy, and are labeled unverified memory rather than evidence. Credential-bearing entries are rejected.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a205e5-07d1-72b3-b0a4-db59d82d43bb","create_time":1795395794.3760543}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":30420,"sampled_through_sequence":30418,"client_authored":false}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T01:03:20.226Z","ordinal":68760,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a205e5-07d1-72b3-b0a4-db59d82d43bb","session_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","root_turn_id":"01a205e5-07d1-72b3-b0a4-db59d82d43bb","response_id":"resp_0f4fd85789ec756b016b0390d1587c87d2987938afda0ed381","usage":{"input_tokens":185345,"cached_input_tokens":183936,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":347,"reasoning_output_tokens":15,"total_tokens":185692},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":5397201,"cached_input_tokens":5206016,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":26386,"reasoning_output_tokens":14042,"total_tokens":5423587},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1451478553,"cached_input_tokens":1439413120,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":2560510,"reasoning_output_tokens":1277346,"total_tokens":1454039063}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T01:03:20.288Z","ordinal":68761,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a205e5-07d1-72b3-b0a4-db59d82d43bb","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-c6d2ac8f-1f13-46f1-b8af-d581c47e4119","changes":{"/home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130/docs/USER_MANUAL.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -768,3 +768,3 @@\n   Servers, plugins, and skills in your home configuration (`~/.config/nexus/`, `~/.nexus/`) are always trusted and loaded.\n-- **Knowledge Graph Hygiene & Auto-Extraction Gating (REQ-SEC-114)**: The `KnowledgeGraph` has a lazy constructor that performs no filesystem creation until a write is explicitly requested. In `--read-only` mode, all mutations are blocked. Implicit standing instruction creation via automatic prompt mining (`autoExtract`) is disabled by default per DEC-15. It can only be enabled explicitly via `NEXUS_KNOWLEDGE_AUTOEXTRACT=1`, which prints a notification whenever a new rule is recorded into `<workspace>/.nexus/knowledge.json`.\n+- **Knowledge Graph Hygiene & Controlled Promotion (REQ-SEC-114)**: The `KnowledgeGraph` has a lazy constructor that performs no filesystem creation until a write is explicitly requested. In `--read-only` mode, all mutations are blocked. Promote durable project knowledge only through an explicit operator command: `/knowledge set <key> <rule>` or `nexus knowledge set <key> <value>`. Model calls to `manage_knowledge` cannot set entries, and the legacy `NEXUS_KNOWLEDGE_AUTOEXTRACT` flag no longer enables conversation-derived writes. Entries are scoped to the workspace, retain provenance and validation status, expire according to their retention policy, and are labeled unverified memory rather than evidence. Credential-bearing entries are rejected.\n - **MCP Server Environment**: MCP servers start with basic process, locale, proxy (`HTTPS_PROXY`, `NO_PROXY`, …) and CA-trust (`SSL_CERT_FILE`, `NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS`, …) variables only — not Nexus's own credentials. Give a server the token it needs in its `env` block in `mcp.json`.\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130/docs/USER_MANUAL.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1795395800284,"completed_at_ms":1795395800288}}
