{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T01:05:20.453Z","ordinal":68869,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a205e5-07d1-72b3-b0a4-db59d82d43bb","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0f4fd85789ec756b016b03914de13087d28ad4f923bdc109e8","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The memory hardening is now implemented on the release branch: model `manage_knowledge` cannot set entries even through its internal handler, legacy auto-extraction no longer writes, and operator-created memory stores provenance, scope, validation state, and retention. Legacy entries migrate as unverified, expired entries are excluded/pruned, prompt memory is explicitly labeled non-evidence, and credential-bearing entries are rejected. The focused memory and trust tests pass; I’m checking the existing operator command and knowledge regressions next."}],"phase":"commentary"},"content_token_count":102,"started_at_ms":1795395917895,"completed_at_ms":1795395920453}}
