{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T01:09:56.297Z","ordinal":68977,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0f4fd85789ec756b016b039262253487d299ac4f2fb3abec86","status":"completed","call_id":"call_8091e89ed2bc40d6afebe0d13c1ac0be","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '18,35p' docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md; rg -n \\\"no reviewed|manage_knowledge also|autoExtract can|no expiry|schema-1\\\" docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md docs/USER_MANUAL.md\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:1500}); text(r.output)\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a205e5-07d1-72b3-b0a4-db59d82d43bb","create_time":1795396194.1472452}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":30515,"sampled_through_sequence":30513,"client_authored":false}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T01:09:56.317Z","ordinal":68978,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a205e5-07d1-72b3-b0a4-db59d82d43bb","session_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","root_turn_id":"01a205e5-07d1-72b3-b0a4-db59d82d43bb","response_id":"resp_0f4fd85789ec756b016b03925ca5ac87d28e822750cb99c38f","usage":{"input_tokens":213121,"cached_input_tokens":212224,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":389,"reasoning_output_tokens":263,"total_tokens":213510},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":10928062,"cached_input_tokens":10704384,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":38370,"reasoning_output_tokens":21722,"total_tokens":10966432},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1457009414,"cached_input_tokens":1444911488,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":2572494,"reasoning_output_tokens":1285026,"total_tokens":1459581908}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T01:09:57.326Z","ordinal":68979,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a205e5-07d1-72b3-b0a4-db59d82d43bb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-9343e9da-7139-4c2f-b279-2dc2e610d0d4","process_id":"5697","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '18,35p' docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md; rg -n \"no reviewed|manage_knowledge also|autoExtract can|no expiry|schema-1\" docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md docs/USER_MANUAL.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '18,35p' docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md","name":"CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md","path":"docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'no reviewed|manage_knowledge also|autoExtract can|no expiry|schema-1' docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md docs/USER_MANUAL.md","query":"no reviewed|manage_knowledge also|autoExtract can|no expiry|schema-1","path":"CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"## Implemented assessment\n\nThe current `/context maturity` output is computed from one content-free on-demand inventory and can change with observed session evidence. On the deterministic command fixture used here, it reports navigability 2 — Exploratory, retrieval speed 2 — Exploratory, freshness 1 — Ad hoc, and compounding value 1 — Ad hoc (no durable memory was present in that fixture). Ratings remain independent and do not claim a managed maturity level.\n\n| Dimension | Current level | Evidence now available | Remaining gap / next improvement |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Navigability | 2 — Exploratory | `/context inspect [--json]` reports stable source IDs, locations, scope, trust, freshness, retrieval reason/method, source counts, and explicit coverage gaps. `SessionManager` persists optional metadata; exports include active and archived source references. | Exact per-inference request manifest and relationships among prompt components are not captured. Capture at request assembly after the `agent.ts` owner handoff. |\n| Retrieval speed | 2 — Exploratory | The inspection command reports per-source and total local collection timings; token counts are labeled client estimates. Source exceptions are represented as failed and gaps are explicit. | No configured deadline, per-inference latency distribution, cache telemetry, or retrieval SLO. Keep this dimension exploratory until request-time measurements and timeout behavior are integrated and measured. |\n| Freshness | 1 — Ad hoc | Items carry explicit `current` / `stale` / `unknown` plus an invalidation rule when freshness is asserted; session and archive reconstruction marks history unknown, and persisted current items are demoted to unknown until revalidated. The live repository-state item is current only at its capture time and names workspace mutation as its invalidation condition. | There is no persisted worktree fingerprint or systematic detector that turns old repository observations stale; future inspections must re-read source state. |\n| Compounding value | 1 — Ad hoc in the no-memory test fixture; 2 — Exploratory only when durable knowledge, notes, or compaction links are observed | Session state, notes, compaction predecessor IDs, and workspace knowledge can be inventoried without copying their text into the inventory. Unverified memory remains labeled unverified. | No reviewed provenance-preserving durable-memory promotion, per-scope deletion/expiry enforcement, or held-out quality evidence. |\n\nRatings are per dimension. There is no aggregate maturity grade. A feature's presence alone does not satisfy a stage: the report requires evidence for shared behavior, freshness, and measured service levels.\n\n## Design decision record\n\n### Decision\n\nAdd a small, local context inventory and deterministic maturity assessment that reuse `AutonomousAgent` getters, `DurableTaskState`/`SessionManager`, existing token estimates, `KnowledgeGraph`, and the common slash router. The inventory stores metadata and token estimates, not prompt plaintext or content hashes. Existing provider adapters remain the only inference transport boundary; this feature does not call providers.\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:95:- Operator-only memory promotion now carries metadata and expiry enforcement, but no held-out task-quality evaluation establishes that durable memories improve results. Existing schema-1 records are migrated additively when a writable load occurs; read-only loads label them in memory without rewriting their files.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":779685404}},"started_at_ms":1795396196546,"completed_at_ms":1795396197326}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T01:09:57.505Z","ordinal":68980,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a205f3-dc81-72e2-9eda-e3eff0d8741d","call_id":"call_8091e89ed2bc40d6afebe0d13c1ac0be","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"## Implemented assessment\n\nThe current `/context maturity` output is computed from one content-free on-demand inventory and can change with observed session evidence. On the deterministic command fixture used here, it reports navigability 2 — Exploratory, retrieval speed 2 — Exploratory, freshness 1 — Ad hoc, and compounding value 1 — Ad hoc (no durable memory was present in that fixture). Ratings remain independent and do not claim a managed maturity level.\n\n| Dimension | Current level | Evidence now available | Remaining gap / next improvement |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Navigability | 2 — Exploratory | `/context inspect [--json]` reports stable source IDs, locations, scope, trust, freshness, retrieval reason/method, source counts, and explicit coverage gaps. `SessionManager` persists optional metadata; exports include active and archived source references. | Exact per-inference request manifest and relationships among prompt components are not captured. Capture at request assembly after the `agent.ts` owner handoff. |\n| Retrieval speed | 2 — Exploratory | The inspection command reports per-source and total local collection timings; token counts are labeled client estimates. Source exceptions are represented as failed and gaps are explicit. | No configured deadline, per-inference latency distribution, cache telemetry, or retrieval SLO. Keep this dimension exploratory until request-time measurements and timeout behavior are integrated and measured. |\n| Freshness | 1 — Ad hoc | Items carry explicit `current` / `stale` / `unknown` plus an invalidation rule when freshness is asserted; session and archive reconstruction marks history unknown, and persisted current items are demoted to unknown until revalidated. The live repository-state item is current only at its capture time and names workspace mutation as its invalidation condition. | There is no persisted worktree fingerprint or systematic detector that turns old repository observations stale; future inspections must re-read source state. |\n| Compounding value | 1 — Ad hoc in the no-memory test fixture; 2 — Exploratory only when durable knowledge, notes, or compaction links are observed | Session state, notes, compaction predecessor IDs, and workspace knowledge can be inventoried without copying their text into the inventory. Unverified memory remains labeled unverified. | No reviewed provenance-preserving durable-memory promotion, per-scope deletion/expiry enforcement, or held-out quality evidence. |\n\nRatings are per dimension. There is no aggregate maturity grade. A feature's presence alone does not satisfy a stage: the report requires evidence for shared behavior, freshness, and measured service levels.\n\n## Design decision record\n\n### Decision\n\nAdd a small, local context inventory and deterministic maturity assessment that reuse `AutonomousAgent` getters, `DurableTaskState`/`SessionManager`, existing token estimates, `KnowledgeGraph`, and the common slash router. The inventory stores metadata and token estimates, not prompt plaintext or content hashes. Existing provider adapters remain the only inference transport boundary; this feature does not call providers.\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:95:- Operator-only memory promotion now carries metadata and expiry enforcement, but no held-out task-quality evaluation establishes that durable memories improve results. Existing schema-1 records are migrated additively when a writable load occurs; read-only loads label them in memory without rewriting their files.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a205e5-07d1-72b3-b0a4-db59d82d43bb","create_time":1795396197.504999}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":30516,"sampled_through_sequence":30513,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
