{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T01:15:57.466Z","ordinal":69150,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0f4fd85789ec756b016b0393c83d4487d2bdc8834c5bb3d0fe","status":"completed","call_id":"call_2b4429df077749c5b7b3ba1c4996652f","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130/docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md\\n@@\\n-| Compounding value | 1 — Ad hoc in the no-memory test fixture; 2 — Exploratory only when durable knowledge, notes, or compaction links are observed | Session state and workspace knowledge are inventoried without copying their text. Operator-only promotion preserves provenance, unverified validation state, repository scope and retention; legacy entries migrate as unverified; expiry is enforced; model writes and automatic extraction are disabled. | No held-out evidence shows persistent memory improves engineering outcomes; the existing store has repository scope only. |\\n+| Compounding value | 1 — Ad hoc in the no-memory fixture and when only a project-knowledge catalog entry is present; 2 — Exploratory only when a durable note or compaction link is observed in carried session context | Session state and workspace knowledge are inventoried without copying their text. Operator-only promotion preserves provenance, unverified validation state, repository scope and retention; legacy entries migrate as unverified; expiry is enforced; model writes and automatic extraction are disabled. | Exact request inclusion and held-out evidence that persistent memory improves engineering outcomes are not measured; the existing store has repository scope only. |\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a205e5-07d1-72b3-b0a4-db59d82d43bb","create_time":1795396552.2412171}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":30592,"sampled_through_sequence":30590,"client_authored":false}}
