35-258): no tool.start/tool.end; the denial is visible only in the next model request and on disk. (3) a forbidden command rule yields a plain failed tool.end; \"denied\" is set only for an operator decline. (4) resume start-up order is hello, history, session.state, notice; a failed resume has no history and a fresh session id. (5) SidecarServer.start() emits hello and session.state synchronously and answers tool.detail/receipt inside handleLine: an in-process link must queue and deliver asynchronously. (6) session.state.workspace is passed through redactPathForOutput: treat a failed realpath comparison on session/load as a mismatch (-32602), not a crash. (7) posture carries no count of extensions not loaded. (8) answering checkpoint.choice with cancel yields error {id: turnId, INTERNAL}; the cause is in the earlier checkpoint.choice.request.message. (9) every sidecar error carrying the turn id ends the turn with no turn.result. (10) the 32 in-flight limit is unreachable with 4 sessions x 1 prompt: test it with an injected lower limit. (11) a real in-process turn costs about 1.5 to 2.6 s: hostile cases not about the sidecar should use a scripted link. (12) safe_text.ts and value imports from protocol.ts pull in ui.ts (ora, picocolors): check before PF-4 exports sidecar_client.ts. (13) commander lets the last repeated option win: forwarded operator flags go BEFORE the adapter's -w/-r, and the link must refuse forwarded -w/-r and a resume id starting with \"-\". (14) receipt_id can repeat across turns (validation receipt id): key the receipt store on session and turn. I hold NO unit claim now. I am still landing #738 and #739 on the owner's explicit instruction to me (\"saying so\", 2026-11-23): #736 is merged (96e96377); I merged the release branch into both and pushed (b40ff965, 55992984).\n2026-11-23T01:10:25Z CLAIM_CORRECTION AC1_ACP_ADAPTER Claude commit 1d62e322 published as PR #740 before takeover; no untracked WIP remained. Follow-up runnable adapter claimed 