{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T01:21:25.524Z","ordinal":69456,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a205e5-07d1-72b3-b0a4-db59d82d43bb","session_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","root_turn_id":"01a205e5-07d1-72b3-b0a4-db59d82d43bb","response_id":"resp_0f4fd85789ec756b016b03951271a087d28504a36fd6d4e98f","usage":{"input_tokens":115418,"cached_input_tokens":115200,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":140,"reasoning_output_tokens":18,"total_tokens":115558},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":21574761,"cached_input_tokens":21193216,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":60640,"reasoning_output_tokens":32103,"total_tokens":21635401},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1467656113,"cached_input_tokens":1455400320,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":2594764,"reasoning_output_tokens":1295407,"total_tokens":1470250877}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T01:21:26.465Z","ordinal":69457,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a205e5-07d1-72b3-b0a4-db59d82d43bb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-37f07068-b3ed-4854-9539-e25dc77f8a02","process_id":"15271","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n \"verification|Current|maturity|compounding|memory|acceptance|agent.ts|pending\" docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md; sed -n '1,260p' docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'verification|Current|maturity|compounding|memory|acceptance|agent.ts|pending' docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md","query":"verification|Current|maturity|compounding|memory|acceptance|agent.ts|pending","path":"CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,260p' docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md","name":"CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md","path":"docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"1:# Nexus context maturity and inventory\n7:Repository: Nexus Code. The initial operator checkout was clean `main` at `9156571f7d5fd8f8436c3105f0237628ab35e857`; the requested implementation target is `release/v1.3.0` at `79ebb92c7254340effd5cd296181794d665648ae`, where this isolated implementation runs on `codex/context-maturity-v130`.\n13:| Navigability | 2 — Exploratory | `AutonomousAgent.requestMessages` carries conversation and pins the durable objective (`cli/src/agent.ts:2318-2338`); `getContextBudget` accounts for messages and tool schemas (`agent.ts:2475-2478`); repository search, skills, and `KnowledgeGraph` exist (`cli/src/knowledge.ts:37-45`, `cli/src/skills.ts:498-518`). | These sources do not have a shared inspectable inventory; the prompt combines several sources and history is replayed as messages. Retrieval reasons and cross-source relationships are not reported together. | Add a common inventory format and a read-only inspection command, while explicitly listing uncovered sources. |\n14:| Retrieval speed | 2 — Exploratory | Deterministic client token estimates, provider-advertised counts where available, admission and bounded compaction exist (`cli/src/tokens.ts:97-158`, `cli/src/agent.ts:3410-3507`). | No source-level retrieval latency budget or SLO is recorded. Admission logs do not measure time spent assembling each source; estimates are not provider measurements. | Record per-source and total inventory-assembly duration; keep it distinct from inference latency and token estimates. |\n15:| Freshness | 1 — Ad hoc | Context is gathered from the live session; candidate/verification evidence has identity-based invalidation elsewhere in the execution model. | Ordinary transcript/tool observations do not consistently carry a repository fingerprint or invalidation rule. Persisted knowledge has timestamps but no enforced applicability fingerprint. Unknown freshness can look current if rendered as prose. | Attach explicit freshness state and source references; report `unknown` where no applicable fingerprint exists. |\n20:The current `/context maturity` output is computed from one content-free on-demand inventory and can change with observed session evidence. On the deterministic command fixture used here, it reports navigability 2 — Exploratory, retrieval speed 2 — Exploratory, freshness 1 — Ad hoc, and compounding value 1 — Ad hoc (no durable memory was present in that fixture). Ratings remain independent and do not claim a managed maturity level.\n22:| Dimension | Current level | Evidence now available | Remaining gap / next improvement |\n24:| Navigability | 2 — Exploratory | `/context inspect [--json]` reports stable source IDs, locations, scope, trust, freshness, retrieval reason/method, source counts, and explicit coverage gaps. `SessionManager` persists optional metadata; exports include active and archived source references. | Exact per-inference request manifest and relationships among prompt components are not captured. Capture at request assembly after the `agent.ts` owner handoff. |\n27:| Compounding value | 1 — Ad hoc in the no-memory fixture and when only a project-knowledge catalog entry is present; 2 — Exploratory only when a durable note or compaction link is observed in carried session context | Session state and workspace knowledge are inventoried without copying their text. Operator-only promotion preserves provenance, unverified validation state, repository scope and retention; legacy entries migrate as unverified; expiry is enforced; model writes and automatic extraction are disabled. | Exact request inclusion and held-out evidence that persistent memory improves engineering outcomes are not measured; the existing store has repository scope only. |\n29:Ratings are per dimension. There is no aggregate maturity grade. A feature's presence alone does not satisfy a stage: the report requires evidence for shared behavior, freshness, and measured service levels.\n35:Add a small, local context inventory and deterministic maturity assessment that reuse `AutonomousAgent` getters, `DurableTaskState`/`SessionManager`, existing token estimates, `KnowledgeGraph`, and the common slash router. The inventory stores metadata and token estimates, not prompt plaintext or content hashes. Existing provider adapters remain the only inference transport boundary; this feature does not call providers.\n42:- `/context inspect [--json] [--record]` measures current client-visible sources on demand and optionally stores a content-free session snapshot; `/context maturity [--json]` emits a deterministic four-dimension assessment with evidence, gaps, limitations, and next improvements.\n48:- No secret-bearing source text is copied into the inventory or maturity report. Paths are workspace-relative where possible. Inventory snapshots follow the containing session's existing retention/deletion behavior; no cross-user cache is introduced.\n52:- Knowledge entries retain repository scope, provenance, validation status, timestamps, and retention policy. Legacy entries migrate additively as `legacy_unverified`; expiring entries are removed from retrieval and pruned on load. Prompt injection labels all knowledge as unverified memory, never evidence. Secret-bearing values are rejected before entering the prompt-visible map.\n60:5. Context inspection and maturity assessment are available through the shared REPL/TUI slash router and JSON output is parseable.\n63:8. Model tool calls and legacy automatic extraction cannot promote durable memory; operator-created knowledge carries provenance and explicit unverified validation status, and expired entries are not retrieved.\n67:- A bounded `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts` boundary request was recorded in the shared claims log for exact per-inference capture at request construction/admission. The file is actively owned by the GV-1 policy-enforcement slice, so it was not edited. Until its owner releases or applies the integration, `/context inspect` is an on-demand approximation and session snapshots remain explicitly partial.\n68:- Automatic memory learning, retrieval ranking changes, and context eviction remain deferred. Durable promotion is operator-only; accumulated memory has not yet been shown to improve task quality on held-out work.\n69:- No Redis, MCP server, vector database, new provider extension, or autonomous memory learner is justified by measured requirements.\n73:XERJ retrieval on `nexus-cli` located the existing context admission/token-accounting path in `cli/src/agent.ts` (`requestMessages`, `admitContext`), the `manage_knowledge` capability (`cli/src/core/capability_definitions/knowledge.ts:23`), and the local project knowledge graph (`cli/src/knowledge.ts:37-45`). OpenCode results showed permission checks belong at the application boundary; Goose results offered no relevant durable-memory analogue. Nexus therefore keeps the existing `KnowledgeGraph`, removes model-write affordances at both schema and handler, and uses the existing operator CLI as the promotion boundary. It rejects a second planner, provider-specific context protocol, external retrieval service, or copied peer implementation. XERJ indexes committed `origin/main`; the active worktree was checked directly.\n77:Implementation worktree: `codex/context-maturity-v130`, based on `release/v1.3.0` commit `79ebb92c7254340effd5cd296181794d665648ae`. The feature branch remains uncommitted and based on that same commit.\n82:| `node --import tsx --test test/context_inventory.test.ts` (from `cli/`, isolated `HOME`/`XDG_CONFIG_HOME`) | 8 passed, 0 failed on current run | Provenance, scope-specific IDs, source failure, deterministic caps, bounded merge, separate/insufficient maturity evidence, common route and read-only policy, no provider call/plaintext persistence, saved-session and archive export. One earlier assertion failed because it matched descriptive metadata; it was corrected to check a unique plaintext sentinel and the rerun passed. |\n90:### Remaining acceptance gaps\n92:- Exact request-time context capture remains pending under an active `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts` claim. A handoff was recorded and the prior GV-1 owner released the memory handler paths; request construction remains explicitly partial until the current agent owner releases or applies that integration.\n95:- Operator-only memory promotion now carries metadata and expiry enforcement, but no held-out task-quality evaluation establishes that durable memories improve results. Existing schema-1 records are migrated additively when a writable load occurs; read-only loads label them in memory without rewriting their files.\n96:- No independent review or full-suite run has been completed; qualification remains pending.\n# Nexus context maturity and inventory\n\nStatus: implemented diagnostic and observability layer on `release/v1.3.0`. It does not replace the agent's request construction or token-admission policy; exact request capture remains a recorded boundary request.\n\n## Baseline\n\nRepository: Nexus Code. The initial operator checkout was clean `main` at `9156571f7d5fd8f8436c3105f0237628ab35e857`; the requested implementation target is `release/v1.3.0` at `79ebb92c7254340effd5cd296181794d665648ae`, where this isolated implementation runs on `codex/context-maturity-v130`.\n\nThe reference is *The Context Engineering Maturity Model: A Framework for Building Production-Ready Agentic Systems* (Redis, 2025/2026 ebook), especially its four pillars and five descriptive stages (pp. 7–16). Nexus uses four dimensions requested for this assessment and adapts the stage language to a local coding client. Vendor architecture recommendations are not treated as implementation requirements.\n\n| Dimension | Baseline level | Evidence and observed behavior | Gaps and limitations | Next improvement |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Navigability | 2 — Exploratory | `AutonomousAgent.requestMessages` carries conversation and pins the durable objective (`cli/src/agent.ts:2318-2338`); `getContextBudget` accounts for messages and tool schemas (`agent.ts:2475-2478`); repository search, skills, and `KnowledgeGraph` exist (`cli/src/knowledge.ts:37-45`, `cli/src/skills.ts:498-518`). | These sources do not have a shared inspectable inventory; the prompt combines several sources and history is replayed as messages. Retrieval reasons and cross-source relationships are not reported together. | Add a common inventory format and a read-only inspection command, while explicitly listing uncovered sources. |\n| Retrieval speed | 2 — Exploratory | Deterministic client token estimates, provider-advertised counts where available, admission and bounded compaction exist (`cli/src/tokens.ts:97-158`, `cli/src/agent.ts:3410-3507`). | No source-level retrieval latency budget or SLO is recorded. Admission logs do not measure time spent assembling each source; estimates are not provider measurements. | Record per-source and total inventory-assembly duration; keep it distinct from inference latency and token estimates. |\n| Freshness | 1 — Ad hoc | Context is gathered from the live session; candidate/verification evidence has identity-based invalidation elsewhere in the execution model. | Ordinary transcript/tool observations do not consistently carry a repository fingerprint or invalidation rule. Persisted knowledge has timestamps but no enforced applicability fingerprint. Unknown freshness can look current if rendered as prose. | Attach explicit freshness state and source references; report `unknown` where no applicable fingerprint exists. |\n| Compounding value | 2 — Exploratory | Sessions, compaction archives and durable task state persist across process restarts (`cli/src/session.ts:102-184`); project knowledge persists in `.nexus/knowledge.json` (`cli/src/knowledge.ts:37-45`). | Session history, task summaries, and repository knowledge have different scopes but no unified provenance/retention view. Knowledge auto-extraction is opt-in and trust-gated, but a stored entry is not evidence of correctness. | Preserve source-only inventory metadata in session records and exports; do not elevate model or tool claims to verified facts. |\n\n## Implemented assessment\n\nThe current `/context maturity` output is computed from one content-free on-demand inventory and can change with observed session evidence. On the deterministic command fixture used here, it reports navigability 2 — Exploratory, retrieval speed 2 — Exploratory, freshness 1 — Ad hoc, and compounding value 1 — Ad hoc (no durable memory was present in that fixture). Ratings remain independent and do not claim a managed maturity level.\n\n| Dimension | Current level | Evidence now available | Remaining gap / next improvement |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Navigability | 2 — Exploratory | `/context inspect [--json]` reports stable source IDs, locations, scope, trust, freshness, retrieval reason/method, source counts, and explicit coverage gaps. `SessionManager` persists optional metadata; exports include active and archived source references. | Exact per-inference request manifest and relationships among prompt components are not captured. Capture at request assembly after the `agent.ts` owner handoff. |\n| Retrieval speed | 2 — Exploratory | The inspection command reports per-source and total local collection timings; token counts are labeled client estimates. Source exceptions are represented as failed and gaps are explicit. | No configured deadline, per-inference latency distribution, cache telemetry, or retrieval SLO. Keep this dimension exploratory until request-time measurements and timeout behavior are integrated and measured. |\n| Freshness | 1 — Ad hoc | Items carry explicit `current` / `stale` / `unknown` plus an invalidation rule when freshness is asserted; session and archive reconstruction marks history unknown, and persisted current items are demoted to unknown until revalidated. The live repository-state item is current only at its capture time and names workspace mutation as its invalidation condition. | There is no persisted worktree fingerprint or systematic detector that turns old repository observations stale; future inspections must re-read source state. |\n| Compounding value | 1 — Ad hoc in the no-memory fixture and when only a project-knowledge catalog entry is present; 2 — Exploratory only when a durable note or compaction link is observed in carried session context | Session state and workspace knowledge are inventoried without copying their text. Operator-only promotion preserves provenance, unverified validation state, repository scope and retention; legacy entries migrate as unverified; expiry is enforced; model writes and automatic extraction are disabled. | Exact request inclusion and held-out evidence that persistent memory improves engineering outcomes are not measured; the existing store has repository scope only. |\n\nRatings are per dimension. There is no aggregate maturity grade. A feature's presence alone does not satisfy a stage: the report requires evidence for shared behavior, freshness, and measured service levels.\n\n## Design decision record\n\n### Decision\n\nAdd a small, local context inventory and deterministic maturity assessment that reuse `AutonomousAgent` getters, `DurableTaskState`/`SessionManager`, existing token estimates, `KnowledgeGraph`, and the common slash router. The inventory stores metadata and token estimates, not prompt plaintext or content hashes. Existing provider adapters remain the only inference transport boundary; this feature does not call providers.\n\n### Data model and interfaces\n\n- `ContextInventoryItem`: stable source-identity id (source type + location + scope; no content hash is persisted), source kind/location, estimated tokens, observed time, freshness (`current`, `stale`, `unknown`), trust state, retention, inclusion reason, retrieval method, and optional source references. Message and tool-call identifiers are retained only as opaque hashes.\n- `ContextInventorySnapshot`: schema version, capture time, session/task/workspace identity, item list, per-source timing/status/counts, estimate provenance, omissions, completeness, and reason for incomplete or unknown coverage.\n- The persisted snapshot is optional. Older session records remain valid; inventory reconstruction labels transcript freshness unknown and marks session-save coverage partial because the exact provider request is unavailable.\n- `/context inspect [--json] [--record]` measures current client-visible sources on demand and optionally stores a content-free session snapshot; `/context maturity [--json]` emits a deterministic four-dimension assessment with evidence, gaps, limitations, and next improvements.\n\n### Compatibility, security, privacy, and retention\n\n- Existing message and session schemas remain readable. New metadata is additive and source-only; full message and tool content remains in the existing session/archive path.\n- Hashes and locators are diagnostic provenance, not proof that a tool observation is true. Model output is labeled model-generated; tool output is labeled unverified unless an existing verifier receipt binds it.\n- No secret-bearing source text is copied into the inventory or maturity report. Paths are workspace-relative where possible. Inventory snapshots follow the containing session's existing retention/deletion behavior; no cross-user cache is introduced.\n- Workspace changes do not silently make an old observation current. If Nexus has no compatible source fingerprint, freshness remains `unknown`.\n- Inventory collection is local and read-only. Failed or unsupported sources are reported with explicit partial status.\n- Durable project knowledge is promoted only through explicit operator commands. Model-invoked `manage_knowledge` rejects `set` even through the internal handler, and the model-visible schema omits that action. Legacy conversation auto-extraction is a no-op, including when its old environment flag is present.\n- Knowledge entries retain repository scope, provenance, validation status, timestamps, and retention policy. Legacy entries migrate additively as `legacy_unverified`; expiring entries are removed from retrieval and pruned on load. Prompt injection labels all knowledge as unverified memory, never evidence. Secret-bearing values are rejected before entering the prompt-visible map.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n1. The same session state yields the same item identities, estimates, assessment levels, and evidence ordering (capture timestamps and duration metrics are the only variable fields).\n2. Inventory content contains no source plaintext and distinguishes operator, model, tool, and persisted-knowledge trust states. A non-unknown freshness claim requires an explicit invalidation rule; persistence or resume without revalidation demotes `current` to `unknown`.\n3. Compaction and resume retain predecessor source references or mark reconstructed provenance and freshness as unknown; exports carry the inventory and archive references.\n4. Synchronous source errors and item caps are visible as incomplete with counts; no partial inventory is called complete. This version has no source deadline and makes no timeout guarantee.\n5. Context inspection and maturity assessment are available through the shared REPL/TUI slash router and JSON output is parseable.\n6. A schema-less/legacy session remains loadable and receives conservative reconstructed inventory metadata.\n7. No provider changes, provider-specific headers, or new service dependencies are added.\n8. Model tool calls and legacy automatic extraction cannot promote durable memory; operator-created knowledge carries provenance and explicit unverified validation status, and expired entries are not retrieved.\n\n### Boundary request and deferred work\n\n- A bounded `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts` boundary request was recorded in the shared claims log for exact per-inference capture at request construction/admission. The file is actively owned by the GV-1 policy-enforcement slice, so it was not edited. Until its owner releases or applies the integration, `/context inspect` is an on-demand approximation and session snapshots remain explicitly partial.\n- Automatic memory learning, retrieval ranking changes, and context eviction remain deferred. Durable promotion is operator-only; accumulated memory has not yet been shown to improve task quality on held-out work.\n- No Redis, MCP server, vector database, new provider extension, or autonomous memory learner is justified by measured requirements.\n\n## Reference coding\n\nXERJ retrieval on `nexus-cli` located the existing context admission/token-accounting path in `cli/src/agent.ts` (`requestMessages`, `admitContext`), the `manage_knowledge` capability (`cli/src/core/capability_definitions/knowledge.ts:23`), and the local project knowledge graph (`cli/src/knowledge.ts:37-45`). OpenCode results showed permission checks belong at the application boundary; Goose results offered no relevant durable-memory analogue. Nexus therefore keeps the existing `KnowledgeGraph`, removes model-write affordances at both schema and handler, and uses the existing operator CLI as the promotion boundary. It rejects a second planner, provider-specific context protocol, external retrieval service, or copied peer implementation. XERJ indexes committed `origin/main`; the active worktree was checked directly.\n\n## Verification evidence\n\nImplementation worktree: `codex/context-maturity-v130`, based on `release/v1.3.0` commit `79ebb92c7254340effd5cd296181794d665648ae`. The feature branch remains uncommitted and based on that same commit.\n\n| Check | Result | Scope |\n|---|---|---|\n| `npm --prefix cli run build` | Passed | TypeScript type-check plus the repository's CLI data/build-info generation steps. |\n| `node --import tsx --test test/context_inventory.test.ts` (from `cli/`, isolated `HOME`/`XDG_CONFIG_HOME`) | 8 passed, 0 failed on current run | Provenance, scope-specific IDs, source failure, deterministic caps, bounded merge, separate/insufficient maturity evidence, common route and read-only policy, no provider call/plaintext persistence, saved-session and archive export. One earlier assertion failed because it matched descriptive metadata; it was corrected to check a unique plaintext sentinel and the rerun passed. |\n| `node --import tsx --test test/session_durable_fields.test.ts` | 4 passed, 0 failed | Session round-trip and REPL/sidecar/ApplicationCore durable-state integration. |\n| `node --import tsx --test test/session_export_escaping.test.ts` | 5 passed, 0 failed | Existing export escaping regressions. |\n| `node --import tsx --test test/provider_wire_matrix.test.ts` | 90 passed, 0 failed | Local mock wire fixtures across built-in and operator-defined provider adapters; no live inference. |\n| `git diff --check` | Passed | Whitespace/error check on the implementation worktree. |\n\nAll TypeScript test commands used Node 24.11.1, one file at a time, with isolated `HOME` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`. The full repository suite was not run. No inference provider was modified or contacted by this feature.\n\n### Remaining acceptance gaps\n\n- Exact request-time context capture remains pending under an active `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts` claim. A handoff was recorded and the prior GV-1 owner released the memory handler paths; request construction remains explicitly partial until the current agent owner releases or applies that integration.\n- No source deadline exists; synchronous source failures and partial outcomes are visible, but this implementation does not guarantee timeout handling.\n- Freshness has no repository/worktree fingerprint or systematic invalidation, and no retrieval-latency SLO or cache instrumentation exists.\n- Operator-only memory promotion now carries metadata and expiry enforcement, but no held-out task-quality evaluation establishes that durable memories improve results. Existing schema-1 records are migrated additively when a writable load occurs; read-only loads label them in memory without rewriting their files.\n- No independent review or full-suite run has been completed; qualification remains pending.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":699251276}},"started_at_ms":1795396885765,"completed_at_ms":1795396886465}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T01:21:26.626Z","ordinal":69458,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a205fe-6062-7f03-babb-c8c651d21a54","call_id":"call_416696a0b9e24731a4cdd487748b1d4d","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"1:# Nexus context maturity and inventory\n7:Repository: Nexus Code. The initial operator checkout was clean `main` at `9156571f7d5fd8f8436c3105f0237628ab35e857`; the requested implementation target is `release/v1.3.0` at `79ebb92c7254340effd5cd296181794d665648ae`, where this isolated implementation runs on `codex/context-maturity-v130`.\n13:| Navigability | 2 — Exploratory | `AutonomousAgent.requestMessages` carries conversation and pins the durable objective (`cli/src/agent.ts:2318-2338`); `getContextBudget` accounts for messages and tool schemas (`agent.ts:2475-2478`); repository search, skills, and `KnowledgeGraph` exist (`cli/src/knowledge.ts:37-45`, `cli/src/skills.ts:498-518`). | These sources do not have a shared inspectable inventory; the prompt combines several sources and history is replayed as messages. Retrieval reasons and cross-source relationships are not reported together. | Add a common inventory format and a read-only inspection command, while explicitly listing uncovered sources. |\n14:| Retrieval speed | 2 — Exploratory | Deterministic client token estimates, provider-advertised counts where available, admission and bounded compaction exist (`cli/src/tokens.ts:97-158`, `cli/src/agent.ts:3410-3507`). | No source-level retrieval latency budget or SLO is recorded. Admission logs do not measure time spent assembling each source; estimates are not provider measurements. | Record per-source and total inventory-assembly duration; keep it distinct from inference latency and token estimates. |\n15:| Freshness | 1 — Ad hoc | Context is gathered from the live session; candidate/verification evidence has identity-based in