{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T01:25:01.382Z","ordinal":69612,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a205e5-07d1-72b3-b0a4-db59d82d43bb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-5721fd9c-862e-47de-b55c-7140f1a0d02d","process_id":"14381","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,62p' /home/mike/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,62p' /home/mike/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md","name":"MEMORY.md","path":"/home/mike/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# Task Group: ai-syndicate consumer lockfile verification and CI phase gate\nscope: Independently audit configured consumer worktrees and lockfiles before a separately gated CI-enforcement phase.\napplies_to: cwd=/home/mike/Projects/ai-syndicate; reuse_rule=read-only audit workflow is reusable; checkout status and configured paths are historical and must be rechecked.\n\n## Task 1: Verify six consumer lockfiles and gate CI enforcement, partial\n### rollout_summary_files\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/mike/Projects/ai-syndicate, rollout_path=/home/mike/.codex/sessions/2026/08/06/rollout-2026-08-06T05-01-32-019fd572-b54f-7672-8626-4c294805393c.jsonl, updated_at=2026-11-20T03:20:47+00:00, thread_id=019fd572-b54f-7672-8626-4c294805393c, phase gate failed)\n### keywords\n- lockfile-verification, six consumers, git status --porcelain, pnpm-lock.yaml, package-lock.json, syndicategate-admin, aisyndicate-ui, phase-gate\n## User preferences\n- For this audit the user required `git status --porcelain`, diff stats, and lockfile diffs for every configured consumer, no consumer mutation, and six explicit results. Preserve read-only scope and report per-repo evidence. [Task 1]\n- “Phase 2 only proceeds if Phase 1 comes back clean” -> stop the later phase on any failed global gate, even when some checks pass. [Task 1]\n## Reusable knowledge\n- Run `git -C <repo> status --porcelain`, `git -C <repo> diff --stat HEAD`, and `git -C <repo> diff -- package-lock.json pnpm-lock.yaml yarn.lock`; record each configured path separately in `design-audit/lockfile-verification.md`. Five accessible checkouts had no lockfile diff, but other worktree changes and one missing checkout failed the gate. [Task 1]\n- Three generated `next-env.d.ts` changes switched `./.next/types/routes.d.ts` to `./.next/dev/types/routes.d.ts`; do not infer ownership or permission to discard them. Report passed `node tools/positioning-lint/positioning-lint.mjs --path design-audit/lockfile-verification.md`. [Task 1]\n## Failures and how to do differently\n- Missing `syndicategate-admin` and dirty/untracked consumer files prevented CI work; preserve the states and clarify the configured path instead of substituting `syndicategate-enterprise/admin-tools` based on its name. [Task 1]\n\n# Task Group: Nexus convergence durable recovery and PR-10 CI integration\nscope: Fail-closed recovered work verification and CI prerequisite integration; release qualification remains a separate gate.\napplies_to: cwd=/home/mike/nexus-code and /home/mike/nexus-wt/p10g-oracle (rollout metadata cwd=/home/mike/Projects/aihost); reuse_rule=recheck current semantics, exact head, claims, and release status.\n\n## Task 1: Align convergence recovery tests, success\n### rollout_summary_files\n- rollout_summaries/2026-10-16T01-45-07-stRS-convergence_recovery_tests_and_pr10_ci_integration.md (cwd=/home/mike/Projects/aihost, rollout_path=/home/mike/.codex/sessions/2026/10/16/rollout-2026-10-16T01-45-07-01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-11-20T03:19:34+00:00, thread_id=01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0, substantive work in Nexus worktree)\n### keywords\n- convergence_integration.test.ts, durable recovery, turnSucceeded, UNVERIFIED, NO_APPLICABLE_VERIFIER, WAITING_ON_DEPENDENCY, SPEC-04, SPEC-11\n## Task 2: Integrate PR #10 CI prerequisite fix, success; release unqualified\n### rollout_summary_files\n- rollout_summaries/2026-10-16T01-45-07-stRS-convergence_recovery_tests_and_pr10_ci_integration.md (cwd=/home/mike/Projects/aihost, rollout_path=/home/mike/.codex/sessions/2026/10/16/rollout-2026-10-16T01-45-07-01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-11-20T03:19:34+00:00, thread_id=01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0, historical integration evidence)\n### keywords\n- PR #10, Node 20/22/24, Linux package reproducibility, check_requirements.mjs, nexus-claims, v1/integration, 2c70d39\n## Reusable knowledge\n- Recovery invalidates persisted verifier baselines; `turnSucceeded` accepts `VERIFIED` or `NOT_REQUIRED`, not `UNVERIFIED`. Preserve resumed conversation and reroute/wait evidence while asserting `BLOCKED` for `COMPLETED/UNVERIFIED (NO_APPLICABLE_VERIFIER)`; independent work can finish while dependent acceptance remains `WAITING_ON_DEPENDENCY`. Focused convergence file passed 5/5 and selected team tests 4/4. [Task 1]\n- Wait for exact-head contract, Node matrix, and dependent Linux packaging/reproducibility checks before integration. PR #10 merged as `2c70d39` after run `39085388798`; at that time requirements enforcement had 12 below-tested rows and version was `0.1.0-alpha.2`. CI integration did not qualify an RC. [Task 2]\n- Shared readiness claims live under `git-common-dir/nexus-claims`; follow `CONCURRENCY.md` ownership and documented 24-hour/dead-PID stale-claim procedure before edits. Related skill: skills/nexus-release-qualification/SKILL.md. [Task 2]\n## Failures and how to do differently\n- Stale A/B/D assertions expected `COMPLETE` after `UNVERIFIED`; update expectations rather than weakening verification. Use precise `NO_APPLICABLE_VERIFIER` rather than describing an unauthenticated baseline when no verifier applies. [Task 1]\n- Merge connector requires `repository_full_name`, not `repo_full_name`. Exact-RC acceptance and other documented release gates cannot be inferred from green integration CI. [Task 2]\n\n# Task Group: Nexus v1.2.x backlog audit and VC-2 shell verification\nscope: Audit v1.2.x backlog and PR gates, and investigate bounded shell snapshots under regression obligations.\napplies_to: cwd=/home/mike/nexus-code and isolated /home/mike/nexus-wt worktrees; reuse_rule=recheck current code, claims, PR heads, hosted checks, and backlog; observed PR status is historical.\n\n## Task 1: Audit v1.2.x backlog and reconcile PR state, partial\n### rollout_summary_files\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/mike/nexus-code, rollout_path=/home/mike/.codex/sessions/2026/11/18/rollout-2026-11-18T21-29-30-01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76.jsonl, updated_at=2026-11-19T20:54:31+00:00, thread_id=01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76, partial; recheck current state)\n### keywords\n- docs/v1.2.2/BACKLOG.md, PR #631, PR #639, PR #642, Entire, apt-get install, invariants, v1.2.x\n## Task 2: VC-2 bounded shell snapshot uncertainty, local fix and open PR\n### rollout_summary_files\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/mike/nexus-code, rollout_path=/home/mike/.codex/sessions/2026/11/18/rollout-2026-11-18T21-29-30-01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76.jsonl, updated_at=2026-11-19T20:54:31+00:00, thread_id=01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76, partial; recheck current state)\n### keywords\n- VC-2, SecurityManager, verificationPaths, unverifiable-change, 64 KiB, 20,000-entry, regression_obligations, verification_shell_guard, PR #642\n## Task 3: Provider tool-call capability warning, unpublished worktree\n### rollout_summary_files\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/mike/nexus-code, rollout_path=/home/mike/.codex/sessions/2026/11/18/rollout-2026-11-18T21-29-30-01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76.jsonl, updated_at=2026-11-19T20:54:31+00:00, thread_id=01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76, partial; recheck current state)\n### keywords\n- p4-provider-tool-support, cli/src/client.ts, content_tool_call.test.ts, tool_choice=required, native calls\n## User preferences\n- Continuation instructions: “completion still requires the requested end state to be true and verified” and “do not redefine success around the work that already exists” -> keep the broader backlog goal active after a partial slice and re-query live state. [Task 1][Task 2]\n- Repository PR text records the owner's direction that missing second-maintainer approval must not block publication; inspect actual automated CI and other required gates, not just an Entire “no reviewers approved” finding. Recheck current policy and branch protection. [Task 1]\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":798643230}},"started_at_ms":1795397100583,"completed_at_ms":1795397101382}}
