home/mike/.codex/sessions/2026/10/16/rollout-2026-10-16T01-45-07-01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-11-20T03:19:34+00:00, thread_id=01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0, historical integration evidence)\n    31\t### keywords\n    32\t- PR #10, Node 20/22/24, Linux package reproducibility, check_requirements.mjs, nexus-claims, v1/integration, 2c70d39\n    33\t## Reusable knowledge\n    34\t- Recovery invalidates persisted verifier baselines; `turnSucceeded` accepts `VERIFIED` or `NOT_REQUIRED`, not `UNVERIFIED`. Preserve resumed conversation and reroute/wait evidence while asserting `BLOCKED` for `COMPLETED/UNVERIFIED (NO_APPLICABLE_VERIFIER)`; independent work can finish while dependent acceptance remains `WAITING_ON_DEPENDENCY`. Focused convergence file passed 5/5 and selected team tests 4/4. [Task 1]\n    35\t- Wait for exact-head contract, Node matrix, and dependent Linux packaging/reproducibility checks before integration. PR #10 merged as `2c70d39` after run `39085388798`; at that time requirements enforcement had 12 below-tested rows and version was `0.1.0-alpha.2`. CI integration did not qualify an RC. [Task 2]\n    36\t- Shared readiness claims live under `git-common-dir/nexus-claims`; follow `CONCURRENCY.md` ownership and documented 24-hour/dead-PID stale-claim procedure before edits. Related skill: skills/nexus-release-qualification/SKILL.md. [Task 2]\n    37\t## Failures and how to do differently\n    38\t- Stale A/B/D assertions expected `COMPLETE` after `UNVERIFIED`; update expectations rather than weakening verification. Use precise `NO_APPLICABLE_VERIFIER` rather than describing an unauthenticated baseline when no verifier applies. [Task 1]\n    39\t- Merge connector requires `repository_full_name`, not `repo_full_name`. Exact-RC acceptance and other documented release gates cannot be inferred from green integration CI. [Task 2]\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":195184820}},"started_at_ms":1795397110890,"completed_