{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T01:48:16.196Z","ordinal":70461,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0f4fd85789ec756b016b039b44846087d2a0e675d6a1f63d7c","status":"completed","call_id":"call_1848a8646aa4448c8ef4a46a4d538c45","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130/docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md\\n@@\\n-Status: implemented diagnostic and observability layer on `release/v1.3.0`. It does not replace the agent's request construction or token-admission policy; exact request capture remains a recorded boundary request.\\n+Status: implemented diagnostic, provenance, and request-observability layer on `release/v1.3.0`. Exact content-free request manifests are captured at the existing adapter-dispatch boundary; they do not replace request construction, token admission, or provider adapters.\\n@@\\n-Repository: Nexus Code. The initial operator checkout was clean `main` at `9156571f7d5fd8f8436c3105f0237628ab35e857`; the requested implementation target is `release/v1.3.0`, initially at `79ebb92c7254340effd5cd296181794d665648ae`. The isolated branch `codex/context-maturity-v130` remains based on that initial release head pending integration with the latest `origin/release/v1.3.0` (`96e963772f36d84561afdca409468f5963746210`).\\n+Repository: Nexus Code. The initial operator checkout was clean `main` at `9156571f7d5fd8f8436c3105f0237628ab35e857`; the requested implementation target is `release/v1.3.0`, initially at `79ebb92c7254340effd5cd296181794d665648ae`. The isolated branch `codex/context-maturity-v130` was rebased onto the current `origin/release/v1.3.0` at `ab7af749b9dd2b6547bd265142d946848d938856`; working changes remain isolated there.\\n@@\\n-| Navigability | 2 — Exploratory | `/context inspect [--json]` reports stable source IDs, locations, scope, trust, freshness, retrieval reason/method, source counts, and explicit coverage gaps. `SessionManager` persists optional metadata; exports include active and archived source references. | Exact per-inference request manifest and relationships among prompt components are not captured. Capture at request assembly after the `agent.ts` owner handoff. |\\n-| Retrieval speed | 2 — Exploratory | The inspection command reports per-source and total local collection timings; token counts are labeled client estimates. Source exceptions are represented as failed and gaps are explicit. | No configured deadline, per-inference latency distribution, cache telemetry, or retrieval SLO. Keep this dimension exploratory until request-time measurements and timeout behavior are integrated and measured. |\\n+| Navigability | 2 — Exploratory | `/context inspect [--json]` reports source identity, scope, trust, freshness, retrieval reason/method, and coverage gaps. Bounded inference manifests reference the exact message positions and tool schemas handed to the adapter; session records and exports preserve them. | Message references identify position and role, not a stable semantic relationship graph. The manifest proves the client-side handoff attempt, not provider receipt or processing. |\\n+| Retrieval speed | 2 — Exploratory | Inspection reports per-source and total local collection timings; outgoing request manifests report client-estimated tokens, configured/advertised limits, and separate token-admission source when available. | No per-source deadline, request-preparation latency distribution, cache telemetry, or retrieval SLO. Do not interpret inventory collection timing as inference latency. |\\n@@\\n-| Compounding value | 1 — Ad hoc in the no-memory fixture and when only a project-knowledge catalog entry is present; 2 — Exploratory only when a durable note or compaction link is observed in carried session context | Session state and workspace knowledge are inventoried without copying their text. Operator-only promotion preserves provenance, unverified validation state, repository scope and retention; legacy entries migrate as unverified; expiry is enforced; model writes and automatic extraction are disabled. | Exact request inclusion and held-out evidence that persistent memory improves engineering outcomes are not measured; the existing store has repository scope only. |\\n+| Compounding value | 1 — Ad hoc in the no-memory fixture and when only a project-knowledge catalog entry is present; 2 — Exploratory only when a durable note or compaction link is observed in carried session context | Session state, compaction links, and bounded request manifests persist source references without copying context text. Operator-only promotion preserves provenance, unverified validation state, repository scope and retention; legacy entries migrate as unverified; expiry is enforced; model writes and automatic extraction are disabled. | Held-out evidence that persistent memory improves engineering outcomes is not measured; the existing durable knowledge store has repository scope only. |\\n@@\\n - `ContextInventorySnapshot`: schema version, capture time, session/task/workspace identity, item list, per-source timing/status/counts, estimate provenance, omissions, completeness, and reason for incomplete or unknown coverage.\\n+- `InferenceContextManifest`: bounded latest-24 session records created immediately before `submitGuardingLength` calls the adapter. It stores message position/role references, effective tool-schema positions/counts, client token estimate, context/output budgets and their sources, optional admission measurement, and dispatch outcome. Prompt and schema text, raw request IDs, model/provider identity, and content hashes are not persisted.\\n - The persisted snapshot is optional. Older session records remain valid; inventory reconstruction labels transcript freshness unknown and marks session-save coverage partial because the exact provider request is unavailable.\\n@@\\n-6. A schema-less/legacy session remains loadable and receives conservative reconstructed inventory metadata.\\n+6. A schema-less/legacy session remains loadable and receives conservative reconstructed inventory metadata; malformed request manifests are discarded.\\n 7. No provider changes, provider-specific headers, or new service dependencies are added.\\n 8. Model tool calls and legacy automatic extraction cannot promote durable memory; operator-created knowledge carries provenance and explicit unverified validation status, and expired entries are not retrieved.\\n+9. A request manifest is durably written before adapter dispatch where the existing durable sinks are available, receives `response_received` only after the adapter returns, and is reconciled to `unknown_effect` after failure or restart before response persistence.\\n@@\\n-### Boundary request and deferred work\\n+### Implemented boundary and deferred work\\n \\n-- A bounded `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts` handoff request was recorded in the shared claims log for exact per-inference capture at request construction/admission. The current claim is associated with PR #738 validation/publication; the owner has been asked to transfer the file or provide an owner-applied integration plan. The file was not edited. Until the transfer or integration occurs, `/context inspect` is an on-demand approximation and session snapshots remain explicitly partial.\\n+- After the owner authorized takeover of stale claims, request capture was integrated at `AutonomousAgent.submitGuardingLength`; the same content-free manifest is saved through existing task/session persistence, exposed to `/context inspect`, and included in session exports. Recovered `dispatching` records become `unknown_effect`; no claim is made that this client-side record proves provider receipt.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a20602-56e4-7401-a61d-85bcc9f8019b","create_time":1795398468.522017}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":31181,"sampled_through_sequence":31179,"client_authored":false}}
