{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:05:17.927Z","ordinal":70984,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a20602-56e4-7401-a61d-85bcc9f8019b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-32ad53da-bd0d-401e-ae59-7db0633e1a99","process_id":"40082","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -i \"context maturity|context engineering|context inventory|memory provenance|maturity\" docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md docs/v1.3.0 docs/releases docs/evidence 2>/dev/null | head -80"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -n -i \"context maturity|context engineering|context inventory|memory provenance|maturity\" docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md docs/v1.3.0 docs/releases docs/evidence 2>/dev/null | head -80"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/evidence/TEST_MATURITY_01.md:1:# TEST_MATURITY_01 — testing-suite maturity evidence\ndocs/evidence/TEST_MATURITY_01.md:3:Slice `TEST_MATURITY_01`, branch `v1/test-maturity-01`, based on `origin/main` at `f3dc49dc`.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.14.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.15.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.4-rc.2.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate. The findings ledger is closed except for the items listed under \"Not closed\"; external qualification is pending. This is **not** a claim that the client is frontier-grade. Supersedes [`v1.1.4-rc.1`](v1.1.4-rc.1.md); everything in rc.1 still applies.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.8.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.3.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.9.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.4-rc.1.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate. The findings ledger is closed except for the items listed under \"Not closed\"; external qualification is pending. This is **not** a claim that the client is frontier-grade: the readiness audit of 2026-11-06 stands, and the measurements it asks for (G1.1-4 on live providers) have not been taken.\ndocs/releases/v1.2.2.md:3:**Maturity:** the implemented v1.2.2 work is listed below. Remaining work and partial limitations are recorded in [`docs/v1.2.2/BACKLOG.md`](../v1.2.2/BACKLOG.md) and under \"Not in this release\" and \"Known limitations\" here. **External qualification is pending.** This is not a claim that Nexus Code is frontier-grade. Every test, scenario and measurement named here is internal validation, and the figures are reported as measured, including the ones that miss. Candidate: [rc.1](v1.2.2-rc.1.md).\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.6.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.10.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.1.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.12.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.2.0-rc.1.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate. Supersedes nothing; the previous stable release is [`v1.1.4`](v1.1.4.md). This candidate carries the whole v1.2.0 scope and the stable release notes ([`v1.2.0.md`](v1.2.0.md)) together, because the release workflow requires a stable tag to be a version-only commit directly on a candidate that already carries its own notes file.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.3.md:3:**Maturity:** Release notes for Nexus Code v1.1.3. This release carries the **entire v1.1.2 scope, unchanged**, under the version number v1.1.3.\ndocs/releases/v1.2.0.md:3:**Maturity:** the v1.2.0 semantic and architectural integrity workstream is landed except for the units listed under \"Not in this release\". **External qualification is pending.** This is not a claim that Nexus Code is frontier-grade. Every test and scenario below is internal validation of this repository's own code; none of it is independent evaluation.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.1.md:3:**Maturity:** Stable release for Nexus Code v1.1.1.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.4-rc.3.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate. Supersedes [`v1.1.4-rc.2`](v1.1.4-rc.2.md). The code is **identical to rc.2** (`cli/`, `core/`, `eval/` and `scripts/` unchanged); this candidate adds the stable release notes ([`v1.1.4.md`](v1.1.4.md)) and the G1.1-4 evidence record, because the release workflow requires a stable tag to be a version-only commit directly on a candidate that already carries its own notes file, and rc.2 does not.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.4.md:3:**Maturity:** the v1.1.4 findings ledger is closed except for the limitations listed below. **External qualification is pending.** This is not a claim that Nexus Code is frontier-grade; the readiness audit of 2026-11-06 stands, and the measurements here are internal.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.2.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.2.1.md:3:**Maturity:** the v1.2.1 plan ([`docs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md`](../v1.2.1/PLAN.md)) is landed except for the units listed under \"Not in this release\". **External qualification is pending.** This is not a claim that Nexus Code is frontier-grade. Every test, scenario and measurement named here is internal validation, and the figures are reported as measured, including the ones that miss. Candidate: [rc.2](v1.2.1-rc.2.md) (rc.1 was superseded: its release workflow failed on a test fixture and published no archive).\ndocs/releases/v1.1.3-rc.1.md:3:**Maturity:** Release notes for Nexus Code v1.1.3. This release carries the **entire v1.1.2 scope, unchanged**, under the version number v1.1.3.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.7.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v0.1.0-alpha.1.md:3:**Maturity:** alpha, pre-1.0 SemVer prerelease.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.11.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:3:**Maturity:** Stable `v1.0.0` was published on 2026-10-31. Publication does not establish completion of the qualification items listed below; those items remain open and are not waived by these notes.\ndocs/releases/v1.2.1-rc.2.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate. Supersedes [`v1.2.1-rc.1`](v1.2.1-rc.1.md); the previous stable release is [`v1.2.0`](v1.2.0.md). This candidate carries the whole v1.2.1 scope and the stable release notes ([`v1.2.1.md`](v1.2.1.md)) together, because the release workflow requires a stable tag to be a version-only commit directly on its release candidate.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.0.md:3:**Maturity: not released.** This document is the release-notes draft for v1.1.0. No `v1.1.0` tag, release candidate or\ndocs/releases/v1.1.0-rc.1.md:3:**Maturity:** Release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.13.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.2.1-rc.1.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate. Supersedes nothing; the previous stable release is [`v1.2.0`](v1.2.0.md). This candidate carries the whole v1.2.1 scope and the stable release notes ([`v1.2.1.md`](v1.2.1.md)) together, because the release workflow requires a stable tag to be a version-only commit directly on its release candidate.\ndocs/releases/v0.1.0-alpha.2.md:3:**Maturity:** alpha, pre-1.0 SemVer prerelease.\ndocs/releases/v1.2.2-rc.1.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate. Supersedes nothing; the previous stable release is [`v1.2.1`](v1.2.1.md). This candidate carries the whole v1.2.2 scope and the stable release notes ([`v1.2.2.md`](v1.2.2.md)) together, because the release workflow requires a stable tag to be a version-only commit directly on its release candidate.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2.md:5:**Maturity:** Release notes for Nexus Code v1.1.2, which ships **with known limitations** that the owner accepted explicitly. They are listed in full below, and the [qualification record](v1.1.2-qualification.md) carries the evidence and the open items. The tag is created after the release pull request merges; these notes describe the source that is tagged.\ndocs/evidence/REVIEW_FIXES_01.md:27:| Evidence/doc drift | Updated TEST_MATURITY_01, INSTALL_BACKUP_01 and DOWNLOAD_PROGRESS_01 to match the code and measurements. |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":775514870}},"started_at_ms":1795399517149,"completed_at_ms":1795399517925}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:05:18.061Z","ordinal":70985,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a20626-876d-7243-8f90-ef8ab9a5326d","call_id":"call_b937d23bd0964c82b373c01dac42d2bc","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"docs/evidence/TEST_MATURITY_01.md:1:# TEST_MATURITY_01 — testing-suite maturity evidence\ndocs/evidence/TEST_MATURITY_01.md:3:Slice `TEST_MATURITY_01`, branch `v1/test-maturity-01`, based on `origin/main` at `f3dc49dc`.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.14.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.15.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.4-rc.2.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate. The findings ledger is closed except for the items listed under \"Not closed\"; external qualification is pending. This is **not** a claim that the client is frontier-grade. Supersedes [`v1.1.4-rc.1`](v1.1.4-rc.1.md); everything in rc.1 still applies.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.8.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.3.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.9.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.4-rc.1.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate. The findings ledger is closed except for the items listed under \"Not closed\"; external qualification is pending. This is **not** a claim that the client is frontier-grade: the readiness audit of 2026-11-06 stands, and the measurements it asks for (G1.1-4 on live providers) have not been taken.\ndocs/releases/v1.2.2.md:3:**Maturity:** the implemented v1.2.2 work is listed below. Remaining work and partial limitations are recorded in [`docs/v1.2.2/BACKLOG.md`](../v1.2.2/BACKLOG.md) and under \"Not in this release\" and \"Known limitations\" here. **External qualification is pending.** This is not a claim that Nexus Code is frontier-grade. Every test, scenario and measurement named here is internal validation, and the figures are reported as measured, including the ones that miss. Candidate: [rc.1](v1.2.2-rc.1.md).\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.6.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.10.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.1.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.12.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.2.0-rc.1.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate. Supersedes nothing; the previous stable release is [`v1.1.4`](v1.1.4.md). This candidate carries the whole v1.2.0 scope and the stable release notes ([`v1.2.0.md`](v1.2.0.md)) together, because the release workflow requires a stable tag to be a version-only commit directly on a candidate that already carries its own notes file.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.3.md:3:**Maturity:** Release notes for Nexus Code v1.1.3. This release carries the **entire v1.1.2 scope, unchanged**, under the version number v1.1.3.\ndocs/releases/v1.2.0.md:3:**Maturity:** the v1.2.0 semantic and architectural integrity workstream is landed except for the units listed under \"Not in this release\". **External qualification is pending.** This is not a claim that Nexus Code is frontier-grade. Every test and scenario below is internal validation of this repository's own code; none of it is independent evaluation.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.1.md:3:**Maturity:** Stable release for Nexus Code v1.1.1.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.4-rc.3.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate. Supersedes [`v1.1.4-rc.2`](v1.1.4-rc.2.md). The code is **identical to rc.2** (`cli/`, `core/`, `eval/` and `scripts/` unchanged); this candidate adds the stable release notes ([`v1.1.4.md`](v1.1.4.md)) and the G1.1-4 evidence record, because the release workflow requires a stable tag to be a version-only commit directly on a candidate that already carries its own notes file, and rc.2 does not.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.4.md:3:**Maturity:** the v1.1.4 findings ledger is closed except for the limitations listed below. **External qualification is pending.** This is not a claim that Nexus Code is frontier-grade; the readiness audit of 2026-11-06 stands, and the measurements here are internal.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.2.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.2.1.md:3:**Maturity:** the v1.2.1 plan ([`docs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md`](../v1.2.1/PLAN.md)) is landed except for the units listed under \"Not in this release\". **External qualification is pending.** This is not a claim that Nexus Code is frontier-grade. Every test, scenario and measurement named here is internal validation, and the figures are reported as measured, including the ones that miss. Candidate: [rc.2](v1.2.1-rc.2.md) (rc.1 was superseded: its release workflow failed on a test fixture and published no archive).\ndocs/releases/v1.1.3-rc.1.md:3:**Maturity:** Release notes for Nexus Code v1.1.3. This release carries the **entire v1.1.2 scope, unchanged**, under the version number v1.1.3.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.7.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v0.1.0-alpha.1.md:3:**Maturity:** alpha, pre-1.0 SemVer prerelease.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.11.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:3:**Maturity:** Stable `v1.0.0` was published on 2026-10-31. Publication does not establish completion of the qualification items listed below; those items remain open and are not waived by these notes.\ndocs/releases/v1.2.1-rc.2.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate. Supersedes [`v1.2.1-rc.1`](v1.2.1-rc.1.md); the previous stable release is [`v1.2.0`](v1.2.0.md). This candidate carries the whole v1.2.1 scope and the stable release notes ([`v1.2.1.md`](v1.2.1.md)) together, because the release workflow requires a stable tag to be a version-only commit directly on its release candidate.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.0.md:3:**Maturity: not released.** This document is the release-notes draft for v1.1.0. No `v1.1.0` tag, release candidate or\ndocs/releases/v1.1.0-rc.1.md:3:**Maturity:** Release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.13.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.2.1-rc.1.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate. Supersedes nothing; the previous stable release is [`v1.2.0`](v1.2.0.md). This candidate carries the whole v1.2.1 scope and the stable release notes ([`v1.2.1.md`](v1.2.1.md)) together, because the release workflow requires a stable tag to be a version-only commit directly on its release candidate.\ndocs/releases/v0.1.0-alpha.2.md:3:**Maturity:** alpha, pre-1.0 SemVer prerelease.\ndocs/releases/v1.2.2-rc.1.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate. Supersedes nothing; the previous stable release is [`v1.2.1`](v1.2.1.md). This candidate carries the whole v1.2.2 scope and the stable release notes ([`v1.2.2.md`](v1.2.2.md)) together, because the release workflow requires a stable tag to be a version-only commit directly on its release candidate.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2.md:5:**Maturity:** Release notes for Nexus Code v1.1.2, which ships **with known limitations** that the owner accepted explicitly. They are listed in full below, and the [qualification record](v1.1.2-qualification.md) carries the evidence and the open items. The tag is created after the release pull request merges; these notes describe the source that is tagged.\ndocs/evidence/REVIEW_FIXES_01.md:27:| Evidence/doc drift | Updated TEST_MATURITY_01, INSTALL_BACKUP_01 and DOWNLOAD_PROGRESS_01 to match the code and measurements. |\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a20602-56e4-7401-a