{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:06:42.893Z","ordinal":71053,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0f4fd85789ec756b016b039fa25b8c87d2899d46655408a13e","status":"completed","call_id":"call_6a26049d25ff42f3830d3685c098c56c","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130/docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md\\n@@\\n | PA-3 | Goal semantics: a ledger entry active from an earlier process resumes **paused** (opencode `goal.ts` boot id), stall counting by failure fingerprint and not turn count, completion decided only by a verifier receipt, an optional token budget rolling up from sub-operations (reference: Codex goal budget); `/team` leaves experimental only after PA-1 and PA-2 | stale goal resumes paused with a visible reason; a model \\\"I am done\\\" does not complete a goal | M | P2 |\\n | PA-4 | **Bounded delegation and workflow commands** (trail 428; [baseline](PA4_BASELINE.md)): extend transient `spawn_subagent` and durable operations with a shared validated delegation contract/outcome, enforce authority intersection and recursive/resource limits, then expose real `/goal`, `/loop`, and `/batch` lifecycles through REPL and TUI/sidecar. Reuse `TeamOrchestrator`, `ConvergenceScheduler`, `OperationStore`, `ResourceRegistry`, specialist profiles, provider recovery, completion evidence, and existing stagnation detectors; do not add a second scheduler or workflow store. `/goal` owns an immutable objective and requirement/evidence ledger; `/loop` is bounded and verifier-driven; `/batch` validates a task graph and maps it into existing work units. Parsing, cancellation, pause/resume, status, recovery, and provider-neutral fixtures are part of each command contract. Spec-format validation may proceed independently; lifecycle and shared-contract work depends on PA-1/PA-2 evidence and WP-P10-02, with `/goal` semantics aligned to PA-3. | prompt-only subagent compatibility; parent/profile/session authority intersection and enforced recursive limits; typed non-success and unknown-effect outcomes; each command has durable state, lifecycle controls, recovery and status through supported interfaces; dependency and workspace conflicts cannot silently complete or overwrite; deterministic verifiers and independent review gate acceptance; standard-contract mock plus existing local/cloud fixtures pass without provider changes | L (staged packages) | P1 |\\n+\\n+### CE: context engineering maturity (new trail, opened 2026-11-23)\\n+\\n+| Unit | What | Accept | Size | Pri |\\n+|---|---|---|---|---|\\n+| CE-1 | Establish auditable context capabilities across navigability, retrieval speed, freshness, and compounding value. Reuse request construction, token accounting, session/archive persistence, path-scoped skills, and the existing project knowledge store. Record content-free manifests for the exact client message/tool arrays sent to adapters; keep source provenance, measurements, scope, trust, and freshness separate; make partial/unavailable context visible; govern durable-memory promotion and retention; produce four independent, evidence-backed maturity assessments. See [`docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md`](../research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md). No Redis, external memory service, provider extension, or new scheduler is presumed. | provenance survives request dispatch, compaction, resume, and export; incomplete sources, stale/unknown freshness, budget limits, and persistence failures are explicit; no prompt/tool plaintext or unverified memory is presented as evidence; scoped memory promotion is controlled; local and cloud-compatible mock adapters run without provider changes; each maturity level cites reproducible client evidence and retains open criteria; qualification includes retrieval latency, freshness invalidation, memory-quality, security, and recovery measurements before any managed/competitive-asset claim | M (staged implementation and qualification) | P1 |\\n@@\\n PA-4 is staged: the existing operation-spec validator can be reused independently; command lifecycles and shared delegation changes follow WP-P10-02 and verified PA-1/PA-2 gates. `/goal` must also satisfy PA-3 before promotion.\\n+CE-1 is a new context-quality trail. Its initial inventory, memory controls, and request-manifest implementation is in progress on `release/v1.3.0`; the remaining freshness, latency, and held-out memory-value evidence stays open until measured. It reuses the existing client and session architecture and does not depend on changing inference providers.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a20602-56e4-7401-a61d-85bcc9f8019b","create_time":1795399586.3596985}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":31442,"sampled_through_sequence":31440,"client_authored":false}}
